<node id="表 1.3">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Table 1.3 represents logical operations and De Morgan's Law.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="表 1.4">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Table 1.4 illustrates the relationship between logical operations and De Morgan's Law.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="DeMorgan's Law">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">De Morgan's Law is a fundamental principle in logic, stating that the negation of a conjunction is equivalent to the disjunction of the negations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="A and B">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The expression 'A and B' indicates that A and B are both true for the statement to be true.&lt;SEP&gt;The logical operation 'A and B' is true only when both A and B are true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="A or B">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The logical operation 'A or B' is true if either A or B is true, or both are true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="not A">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The logical operation 'not A' is the negation of A, meaning it is true when A is false and false when A is true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="not (A and B)">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The negation of 'A and B' is true when A and B are both false, which is according to De Morgan's Law.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="not (A or B)">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The negation of 'A or B' is true when A and B are both false, which is also according to De Morgan's Law.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="A ⟹ B">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The conditional statement 'A implies B' is logically equivalent to 'not A or B', meaning B is true if A is true or A is false.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="If A, then B">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The statement 'If A, then B' implies that B is true whenever A is true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="A only if B">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The statement 'A only if B' means that A can only be true if B is true, and if B is false, A must also be false.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="A is sufficient for B">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A being true is a sufficient condition for B being true, meaning if A is true, B will also be true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="B is necessary for A">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">B being true is a necessary condition for A being true, meaning A cannot be true unless B is true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="A ⟺ B">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The biconditional statement 'A if and only if B' means that A is true if and only if B is true, and vice versa.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="A">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A is a set of vectors that includes a! and a', which form a basis for the column space of the matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;A is a variable used in logical operations and expressions, often representing a proposition or condition.&lt;SEP&gt;A is a variable used to denote a matrix, which is discussed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;A是逻辑命题中的一个假设条件。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="B">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">B is a mathematical entity represented as a matrix of coefficients, which is described as being invertible, and is involved in solving a linear equation system.&lt;SEP&gt;B is a variable used in logical operations and expressions, often representing a proposition or condition.&lt;SEP&gt;B是逻辑命题中的一个结论，假设在A成立的情况下，B也必须成立。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="conjunction">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Conjunction refers to the logical operation that results in true only when both operands are true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="disjunction">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Disjunction refers to the logical operation that results in true if at least one of the operands is true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="implication">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Implication is a logical relationship between two propositions, where the truth of the first proposition (A) implies the truth of the second (B).</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="biconditional">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Biconditional is a logical relationship between two propositions, where the truth of one proposition is equivalent to the truth of the other.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="proposition">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A proposition is a statement that can be either true or false, forming the basis of logical operations and reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="condition">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A condition is a set of criteria or requirements that must be met for a particular outcome or action to occur.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="necessary condition">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A necessary condition is a condition that must be met for an event or outcome to occur, but it is not sufficient on its own.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="sufficient condition">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A sufficient condition is a condition that, if met, guarantees an event or outcome will occur.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="equivalence">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Equivalence refers to the logical relationship where two propositions are either both true or both false.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="equivalent">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Equivalent propositions are those that have the same truth value under all possible conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="logical reasoning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Logical reasoning is the process of inferring conclusions based on logical principles and premises.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="proof">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A proof is a logical argument that demonstrates the validity of a statement or conclusion based on established truths or premises.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="validity">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Validity in logic refers to the property of an argument or statement that guarantees the conclusion is true if the premises are true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="soundness">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Soundness in logic refers to the property of an argument or statement that guarantees the conclusion is true, assuming the premises are true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="inference">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Inference is the process of deriving a conclusion based on premises or evidence.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="deduction">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Deduction is a form of inference in which the conclusion is certain, following logically from the premises.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="induction">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Induction is a form of inference in which the conclusion is probabilistic, based on observed patterns or data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="principle">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A principle is a fundamental truth or proposition that serves as a basis for reasoning or action.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="axiom">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">An axiom is a fundamental statement or proposition that is taken to be true without proof, serving as a starting point for logical reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="postulate">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A postulate is a fundamental assumption or proposition that is taken to be true without proof, often used in mathematics and other fields.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="rule">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A rule is a principle or regulation that governs behavior or action.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="premise">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A premise is a statement that is assumed to be true and serves as a basis for an argument or conclusion.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="conclusion">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A conclusion is the result of reasoning or inference, derived from premises or evidence.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="argument">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">An argument is a collection of statements that are intended to persuade or convince someone of a particular viewpoint or conclusion.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="valid argument">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A valid argument is one in which the conclusion logically follows from the premises, but the premises may not be true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="sound argument">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A sound argument is one in which the conclusion logically follows from the premises, and the premises are true.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</node>
<node id="成立">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">成立是逻辑命题中的一个概念，表示一个条件为真。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</node>
<node id="不成立">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">不成立是逻辑命题中的一个概念，表示一个条件为假。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</node>
<node id="原命题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">原命题是逻辑命题中的一个基础陈述，即如果A成立，则B也成立。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</node>
<node id="逆否命题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">逆否命题是原命题的逆否形式，即如果B不成立，则A也不成立。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</node>
<node id="逻辑证明">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">逻辑证明是利用逻辑规则从已知前提推导出结论的过程。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</node>
<node id="反证法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">反证法是一种逻辑证明方法，通过假设结论不成立来推导出矛盾，从而证明结论成立。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</node>
<node id="直接证明法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">直接证明法是一种逻辑证明方法，通过直接从已知前提推导出结论。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</node>
<node id="逆否命题法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">逆否命题法是一种逻辑证明方法，通过证明原命题的逆否命题来证明原命题。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</node>
<node id="数学归纳法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
