  <data key="d0">variable</data>
  <data key="d1">[0,0, ..., 0] is the zero vector, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="[a1, a2, ..., an]%">
  <data key="d0">variable</data>
  <data key="d1">[a1, a2, ..., an] is a row vector, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="[a1, a2, ..., an]T">
  <data key="d0">variable</data>
  <data key="d1">[a1, a2, ..., an]T is the transpose of a column vector, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="a = b">
  <data key="d0">equation</data>
  <data key="d1">a = b is an equation that represents the equality of two vectors, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="a + b">
  <data key="d0">equation</data>
  <data key="d1">a + b is an equation that represents vector addition, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="a - b">
  <data key="d0">equation</data>
  <data key="d1">a - b is an equation that represents vector subtraction, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="αa">
  <data key="d0">equation</data>
  <data key="d1">αa is an equation that represents scalar multiplication of a vector, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="span[𝑎1, 𝑎2, ..., 𝑎&amp; ]">
  <data key="d0">term</data>
  <data key="d1">span[𝑎1, 𝑎2, ..., 𝑎&amp; ] is a term used to denote the span of a set of vectors, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="linearly independent">
  <data key="d0">term</data>
  <data key="d1">linearly independent is a term used to describe a set of vectors that are not linearly dependent, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="V = span[𝑎1, 𝑎2, ..., 𝑎&amp; ]">
  <data key="d0">equation</data>
  <data key="d1">V = span[𝑎1, 𝑎2, ..., 𝑎&amp; ] is an equation that represents the definition of a vector space, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="dim V">
  <data key="d0">term</data>
  <data key="d1">dim V is a term used to denote the dimension of a vector space, which is discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</node>
<node id="Organization A">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Organization A is referenced in the text as a component involved in a process discussed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Person B">
  <data key="d0">person</data>
  <data key="d1">Person B is mentioned as a figure associated with the text, although no specific description is given.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Geo C">
  <data key="d0">geo</data>
  <data key="d1">Geo C is a location or geographic feature mentioned in the context of the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Event D">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Event D refers to an occurrence described in the text, though no details are provided.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Category E">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Category E represents a type or classification mentioned in the text, but specific details are not given.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Subspace V">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Subspace V is a mathematical concept mentioned in the text, referring to a space where certain properties are defined.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Linearly independent vectors">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Linearly independent vectors are a set of vectors that have the property that no vector in the set can be written as a linear combination of the others.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Span">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Span refers to the set of all possible linear combinations of a set of vectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Dimension">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Dimension refers to the number of elements in a base set of a vector space, which is the minimum number of vectors required to generate the entire space.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Coordinate">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Coordinate is the number associated with a point or vector, indicating its position in a space relative to a chosen set of reference points.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Transpose">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Transpose of a matrix is obtained by reflecting the matrix over its main diagonal, thus turning rows into columns and vice versa.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Dimensions">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Dimensions refer to the number of dimensions or axes in a space, such as the 3D space we live in or the 2D plane.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Measurements">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Measurements are the results of quantifying properties of objects or events, often expressed numerically.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Base transformation">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Base transformation is the change of a basis from one set of vectors to another within a vector space.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Inner product">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Inner product is a mathematical operation that takes two vectors and returns a scalar quantity.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Non-orthogonal basis">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Non-orthogonal basis is a set of vectors that are not at right angles to each other, which affects the calculation of inner products.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Standard basis">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Standard basis is a set of vectors used as a reference in vector spaces, where each vector is orthogonal to the others.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Non-standard basis">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Non-standard basis is a set of vectors that is not a standard basis, meaning the vectors are not necessarily orthogonal.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Degree matrix">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Degree matrix is a matrix whose diagonal elements are the degrees of the vertices of a graph and whose off-diagonal elements are all zero.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Metric tensor">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Metric tensor is a mathematical object used to define the metric in a differentiable manifold.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Scalar quantity">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Scalar quantity is a quantity that is fully described by a single number, independent of any unit of measurement.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="Vector quantity">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Vector quantity is a quantity that has both magnitude and direction.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe522f31b97241ec20aa41e6247bc4a4</data>
</node>
<node id="度量矩阵 G">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The measure matrix G is a concept used to define the inner product between basis vectors in a vector space.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="基向量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Basis vectors are fundamental vectors that define a vector space and are used in constructing the measure matrix G.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="内积">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Inner product is a mathematical operation that takes two vectors and returns a scalar, used in defining the measure matrix G.&lt;SEP&gt;The inner product of two vectors is a scalar value that can be computed from the elements of the vectors and is used to define the angle between the vectors and the length of the vectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="调整后的内积公式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The adjusted inner product formula is a mathematical expression that calculates the inner product of two vectors in a new basis.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="新基">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">New basis refers to a different set of basis vectors used to calculate the inner product in a transformed vector space.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="向量 a">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Vector a is an example vector used to demonstrate the adjusted inner product formula.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="向量 b">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Vector b is an example vector used to demonstrate the adjusted inner product formula.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="矩阵的秩">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The rank of a matrix is the maximum number of linearly independent columns in a matrix, indicating the dimension of its column space.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="线性无关">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Linear independence of vectors means that no vector in a set can be expressed as a linear combination of the other vectors in the set, and they form a basis for the vector space.&lt;SEP&gt;Linearly independent vectors are vectors that cannot be expressed as a linear combination of other vectors in the set.&lt;SEP&gt;线性无关是指一组向量中任意一个向量都不能表示为其他向量的线性组合。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="矩阵 A">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Matrix A is a general matrix used to illustrate the concept of matrix rank and its properties.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="行列式 det(A)">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Determinant of matrix A is a scalar value calculated from the elements of the matrix, used to determine the rank of the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="主子式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Minor of matrix A is a submatrix formed by deleting some rows and columns of A, used in calculating the rank of the matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;Pivot of matrix A is a submatrix that is used to determine the rank of the matrix by calculating its determinant.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="行">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Rows are the horizontal sequences of elements in a matrix, such as the rows of matrix A.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="列">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Columns are the vertical sequences of elements in a matrix, such as the columns of matrix A.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="子矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Submatrix is a matrix formed by deleting some rows and columns from a larger matrix, such as the minors of matrix A.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="线性组合">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A linear combination is a sum of scalar multiples of vectors, which is a fundamental concept in linear algebra and is used to express vectors in terms of other vectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear combination is the sum of scalar multiples of vectors, which is used in determining linear independence of vectors.&lt;SEP&gt;线性组合是指将多个向量按照一定的权重相加得到的新向量。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="操作">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Operations on matrices include addition, subtraction, multiplication, and other transformations that affect the matrix's rank.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="非零标量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Non-zero scalar is a scalar value that is not equal to zero, used in scalar multiplication of vectors to maintain rank.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="列乘以非零标量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Multiplying a column of a matrix by a non-zero scalar is an operation that preserves the rank of the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="列的交换">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Interchanging columns of a matrix is an operation that does not affect the rank of the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="列线性组合">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Performing linear combinations of columns in a matrix is an operation that does not affect the rank of the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="最小非零主子式法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The method of the smallest non-zero minor is a technique used to calculate the rank of a matrix by finding the highest order minor with a non-zero determinant.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="子式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Minor is a determinant of a submatrix of a larger matrix, used in calculating the rank of the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="非零">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Non-zero indicates a value that is not equal to zero, which is important in the calculation of determinants and the determination of rank.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="所有更高阶主子式的行列式均为零">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">All higher-order minors of a matrix have zero determinants, which is a condition for determining the rank of the matrix using the smallest non-zero minor method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de7ae665e4d8bdaf76b458e7dd05332a</data>
</node>
<node id="行列式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The determinant is a scalar value that can be computed from the elements of a square matrix and encodes certain properties of the matrix, such as whether it is invertible.&lt;SEP&gt;行列式是方阵的一个性质，表示为 det𝐴，具有列向量的线性函数、两列相等时为零、单位矩阵的行列式为 1 的性质。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="线性方程组">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A system of linear equations is a collection of one or more linear equations involving the same set of variables.&lt;SEP&gt;A system of linear equations is a set of linear equations with the same number of variables. The solution to a system of linear equations is a set of values for the variables that satisfy all the equations in the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear equation systems are a collection of linear equations with unknowns, which are used to model real-world problems in mathematics, science, and engineering. Solving these systems can lead to the determination of unknown variables that satisfy all equations simultaneously.&lt;SEP&gt;线性方程组是含有多个未知数的方程组，可以用矩阵形式表示为 Ax = b，其中 A 是系数矩阵，x 是未知量向量，b 是常数向量。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47d799488921d39a7d144085504292d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="增广矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">增广矩阵是线性方程组的系数矩阵和常数向量合并的形式，表示为 [A, b]，便于操作。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="rank 𝐴">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">rank 𝐴 是矩阵 A 的秩，表示矩阵 A 的线性无关列的最大数目。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="span[𝑎! , … , 𝑎&quot; ]">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">span[𝑎! , … , 𝑎" ] 是由矩阵 A 的列向量 a! , … , 𝑎" 生成的线性空间。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="dim (span[𝑎! , … , 𝑎&quot; ])">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">dim (span[𝑎! , … , 𝑎" ]) 是 span[𝑎! , … , 𝑎" ] 的维度，即该线性空间的维数。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="解的存在性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">解的存在性是指线性方程组 Ax = b 有解的条件，即 rank 𝐴 = rank [𝐴, b]。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="通解">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">通解是指线性方程组 Ax = b 的解的结构，对于 A 的秩为 m 且 A ∈ ℝ'×" ，则通解可以表示为 x' = B^-1 * b，其中 B 是 A 的一个可逆矩阵。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="最小二乘法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">最小二乘法是一种求解线性方程组的方法，当方程无解时，可以找到残差平方和最小的解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="投影">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">投影是指将一个向量投影到另一个向量的方向上，通常用于求解线性方程组。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="方阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">方阵是指具有相同行数和列数的矩阵，其行列式存在。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="单位矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">单位矩阵是方阵的一种特殊形式，其中主对角线上的元素为 1，其余元素为 0，记作 𝐼" 。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="性质扩展">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">性质扩展是指行列式的性质在特定条件下的应用和推广。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="线性相关">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">线性相关是指一组向量中至少有一个向量可以表示为其他向量的线性组合。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="秩">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">秩是指矩阵中线性无关列的最大数目，也是矩阵的维数。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="系数矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">系数矩阵是线性方程组中未知数系数所构成的矩阵。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="常数向量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">常数向量是线性方程组中与未知数相对应的常数所构成的向量。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="残差平方和">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">残差平方和是线性方程组中误差平方和的一种度量，用于评估解的准确性。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="向量投影">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">向量投影是指将一个向量投影到另一个向量的方向上，通常用于求解线性方程组。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="自由变量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">自由变量是指在解线性方程组时可以任意赋值的变量。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="可逆矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">可逆矩阵是指矩阵的逆矩阵存在的矩阵，其逆矩阵可以通过矩阵乘法求得。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39959957bb3e5b1271426420c0f5629c</data>
</node>
<node id="C">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">C is a mathematical entity represented as a matrix of coefficients, which is part of the linear equation system described in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="D">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">D is a mathematical entity represented as a matrix of coefficients, which is part of the linear equation system described in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="E">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">E is a mathematical entity represented as a matrix of coefficients, which is part of the linear equation system described in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="b">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">b is a vector of constants in the linear equation system, representing the right-hand side of the equation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="a!">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">a! is a vector of coefficients used in the linear equation system, representing the coefficients of the unknowns in the system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="a'">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">a' is a vector of coefficients used in the linear equation system, representing the coefficients of the unknowns in the system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="Ax=b">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Ax=b represents the linear equation system that needs to be solved using the methods described in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="B-1">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">B-1 is the inverse of matrix B, which is used to find the solution to the linear equation system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="x'">
  <data key="d0">person</data>
  <data key="d1">x' is the solution vector of the linear equation system, which is calculated as B-1 multiplied by b.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="min‖Ax−b‖²">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">min‖Ax−b‖² represents the objective of the least squares method, which aims to minimize the sum of the squares of the errors between the observed values and the values predicted by the linear equation Ax=b.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="x*">
  <data key="d0">person</data>
  <data key="d1">x* is the solution vector obtained from the least squares method, which provides the 'best fit' solution to the linear equation system when the exact solution is not possible.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="A% A">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A% A is the product of matrix A with its transpose, which is used in the calculation of the least squares solution x*.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="A% b">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A% b is the product of matrix A with vector b, which is used in the calculation of the least squares solution x*.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="P">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">P is the projection matrix, which is used to project vector b onto the column space of matrix A, resulting in the vector Pb.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="Pb">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Pb is the projection of vector b onto the column space of matrix A, obtained by multiplying the projection matrix P with vector b.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="b-Pb">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">b-Pb is the component of vector b that is orthogonal to the column space of matrix A, which is obtained by subtracting Pb from b.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</node>
<node id="Euclidean Inner Product">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The Euclidean inner product is a specific type of inner product in Euclidean space, where the result is a scalar that measures the "length" of the projection of one vector onto another.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Complex Inner Product">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The complex inner product is a type of inner product in complex vector spaces, involving the conjugate of the second vector.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Positivity Property">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The positivity property states that the inner product of a vector with itself is positive, and zero only if the vector is the zero vector.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Symmetry Property">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The symmetry property states that the inner product is commutative, meaning the order of the vectors does not affect the result.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Additivity Property">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The additivity property states that the inner product is distributive over vector addition.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Homogeneity Property">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The homogeneity property states that the inner product is linear in each argument.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Orthogonality">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Orthogonality refers to the property of two vectors being perpendicular to each other, with an inner product of zero.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Euclidean Norm">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The Euclidean norm, also known as the magnitude or length of a vector, is a measure of the size of a vector in Euclidean space.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Triangle Inequality">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The triangle inequality states that the sum of the lengths of any two sides of a triangle is greater than or equal to the length of the third side, which has a direct application to vector norms.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The Cauchy-Schwarz inequality provides a bound on the magnitude of the dot product of two vectors in terms of their norms, and is a fundamental inequality in real and complex vector spaces.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Real Vector Space">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">A real vector space is a vector space whose vectors are drawn from the set of real numbers, and which is equipped with operations of vector addition and scalar multiplication that satisfy certain axioms.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Complex Vector Space">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">A complex vector space is a vector space whose vectors are drawn from the set of complex numbers, and which is equipped with operations of vector addition and scalar multiplication that satisfy certain axioms.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Vector Addition">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Vector addition is the operation of combining two vectors to produce a third vector that represents the sum of the two original vectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Scalar Multiplication">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Scalar multiplication is the operation of multiplying a vector by a scalar (a real or complex number) to produce a new vector.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Vector Norm">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The norm of a vector is a measure of its length or size, and is a scalar value that is always non-negative.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Negativity Property">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The non-negativity property states that the norm of a vector is always non-negative, and is zero if and only if the vector is the zero vector.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a783ba901d4e86e04fe59c3bba582f2</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑥">
  <data key="d0">variable</data>
  <data key="d1">x represents the vector on the left-hand side of the equation Ax=b, which is being solved for the vector x.&lt;SEP&gt;𝑥 is a variable involved in the text, with the relationship to 𝑦 and the inequality presented.&lt;SEP&gt;𝑥 是自变量，用于表示函数中的输入值。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑦">
  <data key="d0">variable</data>
  <data key="d1">𝑦 is a variable involved in the text, with the relationship to 𝑥 and the inequality presented.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="‖𝑥 , 𝑦‖#">
  <data key="d0">norm</data>
  <data key="d1">‖𝑥 , 𝑦‖# is a norm of the vector (𝑥, 𝑦), indicating a specific measure of its length or magnitude.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="1">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">1 is a constant value in the inequality that relates the norms of x and y.&lt;SEP&gt;1 is the first number in the sequence of numbers used to calculate the values of the matrix A in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;1 is the radius of the open ball in ℝ^3."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The number 1 is mentioned as a constant in the text, possibly serving as a coefficient or a value in an equation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a459a002947ec4863bd1da299f0d036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d615bc2d51e69bb799692bce1003cfb</data>
</node>
<node id="‖𝑥‖">
  <data key="d0">norm</data>
  <data key="d1">‖𝑥‖ is a norm of the vector x, indicating its length or magnitude.&lt;SEP&gt;‖𝑥‖ is the norm of the vector x, which is being minimized in the context of finding the 0-norm optimal solution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="‖𝑦‖">
  <data key="d0">norm</data>
  <data key="d1">‖𝑦‖ is a norm of the vector y, indicating its length or magnitude.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑝-范数">
  <data key="d0">norm</data>
  <data key="d1">The p-norm is a generalization of the Euclidean norm, which applies to vectors in n-dimensional space and is defined based on the p-th power of the absolute values of the vector components.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="Euclidean norm">
  <data key="d0">norm</data>
  <data key="d1">The Euclidean norm is a specific type of p-norm where p equals 2, which corresponds to the standard distance in Euclidean space.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="maximum norm">
  <data key="d0">norm</data>
  <data key="d1">The maximum norm is a type of p-norm where p equals infinity, which is defined as the maximum absolute value of the vector components.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="continuous function">
  <data key="d0">function</data>
  <data key="d1">A continuous function is a function that does not have any breaks, jumps, or holes in its graph.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="linear equation system">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">The linear equation system is an event where a set of linear equations is solved to find values for variables.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="minimum least squares method">
  <data key="d0">method</data>
  <data key="d1">The minimum least squares method is a method for finding the best approximation of the solution to an overdetermined system of linear equations by minimizing the sum of the squares of the errors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="geometric projection method">
  <data key="d0">method</data>
  <data key="d1">The geometric projection method is a method for finding the best approximation of the solution to an overdetermined system of linear equations by projecting the vector b onto the column space of the matrix A.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="‖𝑥 , 𝑦‖">
  <data key="d0">norm</data>
  <data key="d1">‖𝑥 , 𝑦‖ is a norm of the vector (𝑥, 𝑦), indicating its length or magnitude.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="2">
  <data key="d0">constant</data>
  <data key="d1">2 is a constant value in the inequality that relates the norms of x and y.&lt;SEP&gt;2 is the radius of the neighborhood."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;2 is the second number in the sequence of numbers used to calculate the values of the matrix A in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d615bc2d51e69bb799692bce1003cfb</data>
</node>
<node id="‖𝑥, 𝑦‖">
  <data key="d0">norm</data>
  <data key="d1">‖𝑥, 𝑦‖ is a norm of the vector (x, y), indicating its length or magnitude.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="‖𝑥‖ ⋅ ‖𝑦‖">
  <data key="d0">expression</data>
  <data key="d1">‖𝑥‖ ⋅ ‖𝑦‖ is an expression that represents the product of the norms of x and y.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑥$">
  <data key="d0">variable</data>
  <data key="d1">𝑥$ is a variable component of the vector x, which is part of the p-norm definition.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="wxy">
  <data key="d0">expression</data>
  <data key="d1">wxy is an expression that represents the weighted sum of the absolute values of the components of the vector x in the p-norm definition.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="max{|𝑥$ |}">
  <data key="d0">expression</data>
  <data key="d1">max{|𝑥$ |} is an expression that represents the maximum absolute value of the components of the vector x in the p-norm definition.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="∑&quot;$/! 𝑥$#">
  <data key="d0">expression</data>
  <data key="d1">∑"$/! 𝑥$# is an expression that represents the sum of the squares of the components of the vector x in the Euclidean norm definition.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="max |𝑥$ |">
  <data key="d0">expression</data>
  <data key="d1">max |𝑥$ | is an expression that represents the maximum absolute value of the components of the vector x in the maximum norm definition.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="adj(𝐴% 𝐴)">
  <data key="d0">expression</data>
  <data key="d1">adj(𝐴% 𝐴) is an expression that represents the adjugate of the matrix A% A, which is used in the calculation of the inverse of A% A.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="det(𝐴% 𝐴)">
  <data key="d0">expression</data>
  <data key="d1">det(𝐴% 𝐴) is an expression that represents the determinant of the matrix A% A, which is used in the calculation of the inverse of A% A.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="𝐴% 𝐴">
  <data key="d0">matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">𝐴% 𝐴 is a matrix that is derived from the matrix A and is used in the least squares method and the geometric projection method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="𝐴% 𝑏">
  <data key="d0">vector</data>
  <data key="d1">𝐴% 𝑏 is a vector that is derived from the matrix A and the vector b and is used in the least squares method and the geometric projection method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑥 ∗">
  <data key="d0">vector</data>
  <data key="d1">𝑥 ∗ is a vector that represents the optimal solution of the linear equation system in the least squares method and the geometric projection method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="𝐴(𝐴% 𝐴)-! 𝐴%">
  <data key="d0">matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">𝐴(𝐴% 𝐴)-! 𝐴% is a matrix that is used in the geometric projection method to find the projection of vector b onto the column space of matrix A.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑃𝑏">
  <data key="d0">vector</data>
  <data key="d1">𝑃𝑏 is a vector that represents the projection of vector b onto the column space of matrix A in the geometric projection method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑎!">
  <data key="d0">vector</data>
  <data key="d1">𝑎! is a column vector of the matrix A, which is used to define the column space of the matrix A.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑎#">
  <data key="d0">vector</data>
  <data key="d1">𝑎# is a column vector of the matrix A, which is used to define the column space of the matrix A.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑏">
  <data key="d0">vector</data>
  <data key="d1">b represents the vector on the right-hand side of the equation Ax=b, which is being solved for the vector x.&lt;SEP&gt;𝑏 is a column vector that represents the constants in the linear equation system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="𝐴">
  <data key="d0">matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">A represents the matrix on the left-hand side of the equation Ax=b, which is used to transform the vector x into the vector b.&lt;SEP&gt;𝐴 is a matrix that represents the linear equation system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b9498398439c09627a6e6f399f39496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="Matrix A">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Matrix A is a specific matrix used in the discussion of linear algebra problems and is part of the Organization's context.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c07104384db91e0e09863daa1bae3f8</data>
</node>
<node id="Vector b">
  <data key="d0">person</data>
  <data key="d1">Vector b is a specific vector used in the linear algebra problems and is associated with the Person's actions in the context of the Organization.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c07104384db91e0e09863daa1bae3f8</data>
</node>
<node id="Vector x">
  <data key="d0">geo</data>
  <data key="d1">Vector x represents the solution to the linear algebra problem and is associated with the Geo location where the problem is being solved.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c07104384db91e0e09863daa1bae3f8</data>
</node>
<node id="2-Norm">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">2-Norm refers to a specific norm used in the discussion of the linear algebra problem and is part of the Event of solving the problem.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c07104384db91e0e09863daa1bae3f8</data>
</node>
<node id="1-Norm">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">1-Norm is a specific norm mentioned in the context of the linear algebra problem and is part of the Category of mathematics.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c07104384db91e0e09863daa1bae3f8</data>
</node>
<node id="Solution">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Solution refers to the result of the linear algebra problem and is part of the Event of problem solving.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c07104384db91e0e09863daa1bae3f8</data>
</node>
<node id="Equation">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">An equation is a mathematical statement that represents a relationship between two expressions, such as 1⋅1+2⋅1+3⋅1=6, 4⋅1+5⋅1+6⋅1=15, 7⋅1+8⋅1+9⋅1=24.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="2-Norm Optimal Solution">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">The 2-norm optimal solution is a mathematical concept that refers to the best approximation of a vector b by the vector x, in this case, [1,1,1] is the exact solution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="0-Norm Optimal Solution">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">The 0-norm optimal solution is a mathematical concept that refers to the vector with the minimum number of non-zero elements that satisfies Ax=b, in this case, [0,3,0] is the optimal solution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="Linear Transformation">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A linear transformation is a function between two vector spaces that preserves the operations of vector addition and scalar multiplication.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="Natural Basis">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The natural basis is a basis for a vector space, where the basis vectors are the standard unit vectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="Change of Basis">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Change of basis is the process of converting the coordinates of a vector from one basis to another.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="3">
  <data key="d0">number</data>
  <data key="d1">3 is the third number in the sequence of numbers used to calculate the values of the matrix A in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="4">
  <data key="d0">number</data>
  <data key="d1">4 is the fourth number in the sequence of numbers used to calculate the values of the matrix A in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="5">
  <data key="d0">number</data>
  <data key="d1">5 is the fifth number in the sequence of numbers used to calculate the values of the matrix A in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="6">
  <data key="d0">number</data>
  <data key="d1">6 is the result of the first row and first column of matrix A in the text, calculated as 1⋅1+2⋅1+3⋅1.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="7">
  <data key="d0">number</data>
  <data key="d1">7 is the first number in the second row of matrix A in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="8">
  <data key="d0">number</data>
  <data key="d1">8 is the second number in the second row of matrix A in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="9">
  <data key="d0">number</data>
  <data key="d1">9 is the third number in the second row of matrix A in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="24">
  <data key="d0">number</data>
  <data key="d1">24 is the result of the second row and first column of matrix A in the text, calculated as 7⋅1+8⋅1+9⋅1.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="argmin">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">argmin is a mathematical notation that represents the argument that minimizes a given function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="‖𝐴𝑥 − 𝑏‖">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">‖𝐴𝑥 − 𝑏‖ is the norm of the vector difference between Ax and b, which is being minimized in the context of finding the best approximation of b by x.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="Homogeneity">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Homogeneity is a property of linear transformations that states that scaling a vector by a scalar also scales the transformation by the same scalar.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="Additivity">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Additivity is a property of linear transformations that states that the transformation of a sum of vectors is equal to the sum of the transformations of the vectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02fc460eb27b408d6ede2334552d9f4</data>
</node>
<node id="基变换的矩阵形式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The concept of matrix form for basis transformation involves converting from one basis to another using a transformation matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="转换矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The transformation matrix is used to convert coordinates from one basis to another in linear algebra.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="坐标变换的关系">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The relationship of coordinate transformation states that the coordinates of a vector change according to a transformation matrix when changing bases.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="线性变换的性质">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The properties of linear transformations include uniqueness, composition, and invertibility, which are fundamental concepts in linear algebra.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="唯一性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The uniqueness of linear transformations states that a linear transformation corresponds to a unique matrix when a basis is given.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="组合性质">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The composition property of linear transformations indicates that the composition of two linear transformations corresponds to the product of their matrices.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="可逆性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The invertibility of linear transformations refers to the property that a linear transformation is bijective if its matrix is invertible.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="向量旋转和缩放">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Vector rotation and scaling are geometric operations that can be achieved through linear transformations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="坐标变换">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Coordinate transformation is the process of switching coordinates between different bases, used in graphics and physics.&lt;SEP&gt;Coordinate transformation refers to the process of changing the coordinates of a point or system from one coordinate system to another.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="多维数据变换">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Multidimensional data transformation refers to the use of linear transformations in machine learning and data analysis for feature space transformation and dimensionality reduction.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征值的存在条件">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The existence conditions of eigenvalues require that the matrix (λI - A) be singular (non-invertible) for λ to be an eigenvalue.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征方程">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The characteristic equation is a polynomial equation det(λI - A) = 0 that is used to find eigenvalues of a matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征多项式与特征方程">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The characteristic polynomial is the polynomial det(λI - A) = 0, and its roots are the eigenvalues of the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征值和特征向量的性质">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The properties of eigenvalues and eigenvectors include linear independence and diagonalization of matrices.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="线性无关性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The linear independence of eigenvalues and eigenvectors states that if the eigenvalues are distinct, the corresponding eigenvectors are linearly independent.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="矩阵对角化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Matrix diagonalization is the process of converting a matrix into a diagonal matrix using its eigenvalues and eigenvectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="对称矩阵的特征值与特征向量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The eigenvalues of a symmetric matrix are all real numbers, and the eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues are orthogonal.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="矩阵形式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The term 'matrix form' refers to the representation of data or a mathematical object as a matrix, typically used in linear algebra.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="线性代数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Linear algebra is a branch of mathematics that deals with vectors, matrices, and linear transformations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实方阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A real square matrix is a matrix that is square (the number of rows is equal to the number of columns) and has real numbers as its elements.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="非零向量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A non-zero vector is a vector with a magnitude that is not zero, which is essential for the definition of eigenvalues and eigenvectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="矩阵方程">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A matrix equation involves matrices and their elements in an equation, typically used in solving systems of linear equations or finding eigenvalues/eigenvectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征值">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">An eigenvalue is a scalar associated with a linear transformation that is equal to the factor by which an eigenvector is scaled when transformed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征向量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">An eigenvector is a vector associated with an eigenvalue, which remains in the same direction after the linear transformation is applied to it.&lt;SEP&gt;Each eigenvalue of a matrix has at least one corresponding eigenvector, which is a non-zero vector that, when multiplied by the matrix, results in a scalar multiple of itself.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="奇异矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A singular matrix is a square matrix that is non-invertible, meaning its determinant is zero and it does not have an inverse matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="不可逆矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">An non-invertible matrix, also known as a singular matrix, does not have a matrix inverse, and its determinant is zero.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="多项式方程">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A polynomial equation is an equation that consists of variables and coefficients, and the highest degree of the variable is non-negative.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征多项式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The characteristic polynomial is a polynomial whose coefficients are determined by the elements of a matrix and whose roots are the eigenvalues of the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="对称矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A square matrix is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose. This property is significant in linear algebra, particularly in the context of orthogonal matrices and projection matrices.&lt;SEP&gt;A symmetric matrix is a square matrix that is equal to its transpose, and it has real eigenvalues and orthogonal eigenvectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0bce880b9d8eb573945d1e3eb7bec38</data>
</node>
<node id="正交性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Orthogonality refers to the property of vectors that are perpendicular to each other in a real inner product space, which is a generalization of perpendicularity in Euclidean space.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Real numbers are numbers that can be represented on a number line and include all rational and irrational numbers.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="复数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Complex numbers are numbers that consist of a real part and an imaginary part, and they are represented as a + bi, where a and b are real numbers and i is the imaginary unit.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="向量空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A vector space is a collection of vectors that can be scaled and added together according to certain rules.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="线性空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A linear space, also called a vector space, is a collection of vectors that can be scaled and added according to certain rules.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="欧几里得空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The Euclidean space is a type of inner product space that is often used to represent physical space and has the familiar properties of distance and angle.&lt;SEP&gt;欧几里得空间是一个几何空间，其中任意两点之间的线段都存在。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="维度">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Dimension refers to the number of coordinates needed to specify a point uniquely in a space, such as in a coordinate system.&lt;SEP&gt;维度是超平面的属性，表示超平面的自由度。"&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d615bc2d51e69bb799692bce1003cfb</data>
</node>
<node id="特征多项式的根">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The roots of the characteristic polynomial are the eigenvalues of the matrix, which are scalar values associated with eigenvectors that are scaled by the linear transformation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="矩阵的对角化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Matrix diagonalization is a process of converting a matrix into a diagonal matrix using its eigenvalues and eigenvectors, which is useful in solving systems of linear equations and other problems in linear algebra.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="相似矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Similar matrices are matrices that can be transformed into each other by a similarity transformation, which is a type of linear transformation that preserves the eigenvalues of the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="正交矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">An orthogonal matrix is a square matrix whose columns and rows are orthogonal unit vectors, and its inverse is equal to its transpose.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="幂零矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A nilpotent matrix is a square matrix N such that N^k = 0 for some positive integer k, which means that repeated application of the matrix eventually results in the zero matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="矩阵乘法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Matrix multiplication is an operation that combines two matrices to produce a third matrix, which is used to solve systems of linear equations and perform various calculations in linear algebra.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="行列式的值">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The value of the determinant is a scalar that can be computed from the elements of a square matrix and is used to determine whether the matrix is invertible and to solve systems of linear equations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="齐次线性方程组">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A system of homogeneous linear equations is a system where all the constant terms are zero, and the solutions form a vector space that includes the zero vector.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="非齐次线性方程组">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A system of non-homogeneous linear equations is a system where at least one constant term is non-zero, and the solutions may not include the zero vector.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征多项式的次数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The degree of the characteristic polynomial is equal to the size of the matrix, which is the number of rows and columns in the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征向量的线性组合">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The linear combination of eigenvectors refers to expressing eigenvectors as a sum of other eigenvectors with different eigenvalues, which is possible in the case of distinct eigenvalues.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="矩阵的特征值和特征向量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a matrix are properties of the matrix that relate to its linear transformation and can be used to understand the matrix's behavior and properties.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征值的几何意义">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The geometric meaning of eigenvalues relates to the scaling factor by which eigenvectors are stretched or shrunk when transformed by the linear transformation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="特征向量的几何意义">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The geometric meaning of eigenvectors relates to the directions in which eigenvectors are stretched or shrunk when transformed by the linear transformation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的正定性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The positive definiteness of a real symmetric matrix refers to its property that all its eigenvalues are positive, which implies that the matrix is invertible and the quadratic form associated with it is always positive.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的负定性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The negative definiteness of a real symmetric matrix refers to its property that all its eigenvalues are negative, which implies that the matrix is invertible and the quadratic form associated with it is always negative.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的半正定性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The semi-positive definiteness of a real symmetric matrix refers to its property that all its eigenvalues are non-negative, which implies that the matrix is invertible and the quadratic form associated with it is non-negative.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的半负定性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The semi-negative definiteness of a real symmetric matrix refers to its property that all its eigenvalues are non-positive, which implies that the matrix is invertible and the quadratic form associated with it is non-positive.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的自伴性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The self-adjointness of a real symmetric matrix refers to its property that it is equal to its conjugate transpose, which is a key property for diagonalization and other applications.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的正惯性指数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The positive inertia index of a real symmetric matrix is a measure of the number of positive eigenvalues, which is useful in determining the properties of the quadratic form associated with the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的负惯性指数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The negative inertia index of a real symmetric matrix is a measure of the number of negative eigenvalues, which is useful in determining the properties of the quadratic form associated with the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的零惯性指数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The zero inertia index of a real symmetric matrix is a measure of the number of zero eigenvalues, which is useful in determining the properties of the quadratic form associated with the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的迹">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The trace of a real symmetric matrix is the sum of its diagonal elements, which is an important property for diagonalization and other applications.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的行列式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The determinant of a real symmetric matrix is a scalar value that can be computed from the elements of the matrix and is used to determine whether the matrix is invertible.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的特征值和特征向量的正负">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The sign of the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a real symmetric matrix indicates whether the matrix is positive definite, negative definite, or semi-definite.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的对角化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The diagonalization of a real symmetric matrix involves finding a diagonal matrix and an invertible matrix such that the original matrix is equal to the product of the two matrices.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的特征多项式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The characteristic polynomial of a real symmetric matrix is a polynomial equation whose roots are the eigenvalues of the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的特征方程">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The characteristic equation of a real symmetric matrix is a polynomial equation that is used to find the eigenvalues of the matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的特征值的存在性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The existence of eigenvalues of a real symmetric matrix is guaranteed by the fact that the matrix is diagonalizable, meaning it can be expressed as a diagonal matrix using its eigenvalues and eigenvectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的特征向量的存在性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The existence of eigenvectors of a real symmetric matrix is guaranteed by the fact that the matrix is diagonalizable, meaning it can be expressed as a diagonal matrix using its eigenvalues and eigenvectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的特征值的唯一性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The uniqueness of eigenvalues of a real symmetric matrix is guaranteed by the fact that the matrix is diagonalizable, meaning it can be expressed as a diagonal matrix using its eigenvalues and eigenvectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的特征向量的唯一性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The uniqueness of eigenvectors of a real symmetric matrix is guaranteed by the fact that the matrix is diagonalizable, meaning it can be expressed as a diagonal matrix using its eigenvalues and eigenvectors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的特征值的实数性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The eigenvalues of a real symmetric matrix are always real numbers, which is a key property that distinguishes them from complex eigenvalues in general matrices.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的特征向量的正交性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The eigenvectors of a real symmetric matrix corresponding to different eigenvalues are orthogonal to each other, which is a key property for diagonalization and other applications.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6197a591a9e3c0503fa926a264b6253d</data>
</node>
<node id="实对称矩阵的特征向量的单位性">
