<node id="直和">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The direct sum is a concept in linear algebra that combines two vector spaces into a new one without losing any elements. It is used to describe the decomposition of a vector space into a sum of subspaces.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0bce880b9d8eb573945d1e3eb7bec38</data>
</node>
<node id="幂等矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A square matrix that, when multiplied by itself, yields itself is called a幂等矩阵. It is a key property of projection matrices in linear algebra.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0bce880b9d8eb573945d1e3eb7bec38</data>
</node>
<node id="零空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The null space of a matrix is the set of vectors that, when multiplied by the matrix, result in the zero vector. It is a fundamental concept in linear algebra, particularly in the context of linear transformations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0bce880b9d8eb573945d1e3eb7bec38</data>
</node>
<node id="列空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The column space of a matrix is the span of its column vectors. It is a fundamental concept in linear algebra, representing the subspace that the matrix maps into.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0bce880b9d8eb573945d1e3eb7bec38</data>
</node>
<node id="最小二乘问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The least squares problem is a method to find the best fit for a set of data, minimizing the sum of the squares of the differences between the observed values and the values predicted by the model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0bce880b9d8eb573945d1e3eb7bec38</data>
</node>
<node id="信号处理">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Signal processing involves the analysis, modification, and synthesis of signals. It is an interdisciplinary field that covers many areas of science and engineering, including electrical engineering, computer science, and physics. Signal processing is used in a wide variety of applications, such as audio and image processing, telecommunications, and medical imaging.&lt;SEP&gt;Signal processing is a field of engineering that focuses on the analysis, modification, and synthesis of signals. It is used in various applications, including audio and image processing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0bce880b9d8eb573945d1e3eb7bec38</data>
