</node>
<node id="运筹学与经济学">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">运筹学与经济学是数学的一个分支，使用凸集来描述生产可能性集合、预算约束和市场均衡。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">空间指的是任何存在物体的区域，可以是二维的、三维的，甚至是更高维度的空间。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="点">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">点是最基本的几何对象，没有大小，仅有位置。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="正半空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">正半空间是指超平面的一侧，满足超平面方程的点的集合。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="负半空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">负半空间是指超平面的另一侧，满足超平面方程的点的集合。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="点 P(2,1)">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">点 P(2,1) 是一个二维空间中的点，其坐标为 (2,1)。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="决策边界">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">决策边界是分类问题中的超平面，用于将数据分为不同的类别。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="样本点">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">样本点是指数据集中的单个数据点，用于训练和支持向量机等分类算法。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="标签">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">标签是分类问题中的术语，用于标识数据点属于哪个类别。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="分类面">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">分类面是支持向量机中的超平面，用于在数据集上做出分类决策。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="欧几里得距离">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">欧几里得距离是测量两点之间距离的一种方式，适用于欧几里得空间。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="最优解">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">最优解是优化问题中的解，它满足问题的所有约束条件，并且是最优的。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="生产可能性集合">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">生产可能性集合是运筹学与经济学中的一个概念，表示一个经济系统可能生产的所有商品和服务的组合。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="预算约束">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">预算约束是经济学中的一个概念，表示一个个体或组织可用的资源总量。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="市场均衡">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">市场均衡是经济学中的一个概念，表示市场上供给和需求达到平衡的状态。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="交集">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">交集是指两个或多个集合共有的元素组成的集合。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="凸包 (Convex Hull)">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">凸包是一个数学概念，用来表示一个非凸集合的最小凸包含。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="凸函数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">凸函数是一个数学函数，其图像在定义域内是凸的。&lt;SEP&gt;凸函数是具有特定性质的函数，其图形是向上凸的，用于凸优化问题。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="稳定性区域">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">稳定性区域是控制理论中的一个概念，表示系统可能稳定运行的区域。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="形状拟合">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">形状拟合是图像处理中的一个任务，用于识别和描述图像中的形状。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="生产可能性边界">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">生产可能性边界是运筹学与经济学中的一个概念，表示生产可能性集合的边界。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="消费可能性边界">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">消费可能性边界是运筹学与经济学中的一个概念，表示消费者在预算约束下的消费组合边界。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d63c0ad8afdfdcb8edc241ea203de7b1</data>
</node>
<node id="几何特性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The geometric characteristics mentioned refer to the properties of shapes and their analysis in data processing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="凸性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Convexity refers to the property of a set where any line segment connecting two points within the set lies entirely within the set itself.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="凸集理论">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Convex set theory is a branch of mathematics that deals with the study of convex sets and their properties.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="非凸问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Non-convex problems refer to problems where the feasible region is not a convex set, which makes them more complex to solve.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="全局最优问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Global optimization problems seek to find the best solution among all possible solutions to a problem.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="高维空间复杂性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">High-dimensional space complexity refers to the computational difficulty and representation issues associated with high-dimensional data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="复杂形状">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Complex shapes refer to shapes with indentations or irregular boundaries that cannot be accurately described by convex sets.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="二维平面">
  <data key="d0">geo</data>
  <data key="d1">A two-dimensional plane is a flat surface that is used to represent and analyze geometric shapes and their properties.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="凸多边形">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A convex polygon is a polygon where all the interior angles are less than 180 degrees, and the line segments connecting vertices lie entirely within the polygon.&lt;SEP&gt;A convex polygon is a simple polygon in which no line segment between two points on the polygon intersects the polygon interior. It is a two-dimensional convex set.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="三维凸球体">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A three-dimensional convex sphere is a shape where every point on the surface is equidistant from a fixed center point.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="线性约束的可行域">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The feasible region defined by linear constraints is the set of all points that satisfy the given constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="一维空间">
  <data key="d0">geo</data>
  <data key="d1">One-dimensional space is a space that is defined by a single real number line.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="高维空间">
  <data key="d0">geo</data>
  <data key="d1">High-dimensional space is a space that has more than three dimensions, which can be challenging to visualize or understand.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="拓扑学">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Topology is a branch of mathematics that studies the properties of spaces that are preserved under continuous deformations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="机器学习">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Machine learning is a field of computer science that uses algorithms and statistical models to enable computers to improve their performance on specific tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine learning is an application field of optimization, used for optimizing loss functions and training deep learning models.&lt;SEP&gt;文中提到的机器学习，可能指利用数据训练模型的技术。&lt;SEP&gt;机器学习是研究如何让计算机从数据中学习并做出决策的学科。"&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5b9cad1a482c29a56b35fc8a645c21c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d615bc2d51e69bb799692bce1003cfb</data>
</node>
<node id="最优化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Optimization is the process of finding the best solution among all possible solutions to a problem, often with constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="数值分析">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Numerical analysis is a branch of mathematics that studies methods for solving mathematical problems using numerical approximation techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;文中涉及的领域，数值分析是研究数值计算的理论和方法。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5b9cad1a482c29a56b35fc8a645c21c</data>
</node>
<node id="数据分析">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Data analysis is the process of inspecting and modeling data to discover useful information, suggesting conclusions, and supporting decision-making.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="缺点">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Disadvantages refer to the negative aspects or limitations of a concept, method, or system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="局限性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Limitations are restrictions or boundaries that prevent something from being fully effective or achieving its full potential.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="表示方式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Representation refers to the method or form in which something is expressed or depicted.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="凹陷或不规则边界">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Indents or irregular boundaries refer to shapes that have indentations or lack regular edges.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="例 1: 二维平面中的凸多边形 - 顶点">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The vertices of a convex polygon in a two-dimensional plane are the points that define its shape.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="例 2: 三维凸球体 - 球心">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The center of a three-dimensional convex sphere is the fixed point from which all points on the surface are equidistant.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="例 3: 线性约束的可行域 - 约束条件">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Constraint conditions in the feasible region defined by linear constraints are the rules that limit the possible solutions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="邻域的定义 - 𝜀-邻域">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The 𝜀-neighborhood is a set of points around a given point in a metric space that are within a certain distance 𝜀 from the point.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="邻域的几何意义 - 一维空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">In one-dimensional space, a neighborhood is an interval around a point with a given radius 𝜀.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="邻域的几何意义 - 二维空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">In two-dimensional space, a neighborhood is a circle around a point with a given radius 𝜀.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="邻域的几何意义 - 高维空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">In high-dimensional space, a neighborhood is a hypersphere around a point with a given radius 𝜀.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="邻域的性质 - 开放性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Openness of a neighborhood refers to the property that no boundary points are included in the neighborhood.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="邻域的性质 - 任意小性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The property of arbitrary smallness of a neighborhood means that for any positive number 𝜀, there is a neighborhood around the point.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="邻域的性质 - 点覆盖性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Point coverability of a neighborhood refers to the property that the point is the center of the neighborhood and can be covered by it.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="应用 - 拓扑学">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">In topology, neighborhoods are used to define open sets, closed sets, and limit points.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="应用 - 机器学习">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">In machine learning, neighborhoods are used in algorithms like k-nearest neighbors to define local relationships between points.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="应用 - 最优化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">In optimization, neighborhoods are used in trust-region methods to solve nonlinear optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="应用 - 物理模拟">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">In physical simulations, neighborhoods are used to define the range of interaction between particles.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="应用 - 数值分析">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">In numerical analysis, neighborhoods are used to study the convergence and error analysis of numerical methods.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="优点 - 适用性强">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The strong applicability of neighborhoods refers to their ability to be used in any Euclidean space of any dimension.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="优点 - 拓扑基础">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Neighborhoods have a topological foundation and are an important tool in topology.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="优点 - 分析功能">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Neighborhoods have analytical functions and are used in calculus and analysis to define continuity, differentiability, and convergence.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="优点 - 几何直观">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The geometric intuition of neighborhoods, such as spheres and circles, is easy to understand and visualize.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="缺点 - 复杂性随着维度增加">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The complexity of neighborhoods increases with the dimension, making their geometric structure less intuitive.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="缺点 - 依赖度量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Neighborhoods depend on the metric, and if the metric changes, the shape of the neighborhood will also change.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="缺点 - 理论性较强">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The topological properties of neighborhoods are theoretically strong but may not be intuitive for practical operations in application domains.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="一维空间中的邻域 - 𝜀-邻域">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The 𝜀-neighborhood in one-dimensional space is an interval (𝑥: − 𝜀, 𝑥: + 𝜀) around a point 𝑥: with a given radius 𝜀.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="二维空间中的邻域 - 𝜀-邻域">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The 𝜀-neighborhood in two-dimensional space is a circle (𝑁# ((1,1)) = {(𝑥! , 𝑥# ) ∈ ℝ# : r(𝑥! − 1)# + (𝑥# − 1)# &lt; 2}) around a point (1,1) with a given radius 𝜀.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7cc076d41604c34f64fbfa9e6c4efba9</data>
</node>
<node id="ℝ# 平面">
  <data key="d0">geo</data>
  <data key="d1">ℝ# 平面是一个二维几何空间，用于定义点 (1,1) 和其邻域。"&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d615bc2d51e69bb799692bce1003cfb</data>
</node>
<node id="(1,1)">
  <data key="d0">geo</data>
