</node>
<node id="优化目标">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The optimization goal is to find the vertex solutions under the linear objective function in the constrained conditions of linear programming.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="序列">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A sequence is an ordered collection of elements. A sequence can be finite or infinite. The elements of a sequence are called terms. A sequence is said to be convergent if it approaches a finite limit as the number of terms approaches infinity, and divergent if it does not. A sequence is said to be oscillating if it does not approach a finite limit and instead oscillates between two or more values.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="极限">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The limit of a sequence is the value that the terms of the sequence tend to approach as the number of terms goes to infinity. A sequence is convergent if it has a limit, and divergent if it does not. A sequence is said to be oscillating if it does not approach a finite limit and instead oscillates between two or more values.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="收敛序列">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A convergent sequence is a sequence whose terms approach a finite limit as the number of terms goes to infinity. The limit of a convergent sequence is called its limit.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="发散序列">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A divergent sequence is a sequence whose terms do not approach a finite limit as the number of terms goes to infinity. A sequence is divergent if it does not converge to a finite limit.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="震荡序列">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">An oscillating sequence is a sequence whose terms do not approach a finite limit and instead oscillate between two or more values. It is a sequence that does not converge to a finite limit and does not diverge to infinity.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="机器学习与优化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Machine learning and optimization involve the use of mathematical optimization techniques in machine learning to find the best model for a given dataset. Optimization techniques are used to minimize or maximize an objective function, often with constraints. These techniques are crucial in various machine learning applications such as clustering, regression, and classification.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="数值分析与计算">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Numerical analysis and computation involve the study of algorithms and methods for solving mathematical problems using numerical approximation. Numerical analysis is an area of mathematics that studies methods for solving mathematical problems that are often too complex to solve exactly.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="物理与工程">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Physics and engineering involve the application of mathematical and scientific principles to solve real-world problems. In physics, the focus is on understanding the natural world, while in engineering, the focus is on designing and constructing useful objects. Both fields rely heavily on mathematics and science.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="经济学与金融学">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Economics and finance involve the application of mathematical and statistical methods to analyze economic phenomena and make financial decisions. Economics is the social science that studies the production, distribution, and consumption of goods and services. Finance is the field of study concerned with the management of money and other assets. Both fields rely heavily on mathematics and statistics.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="约束条件">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Constraints are conditions or limitations that must be satisfied in order to find a solution to a problem. In linear programming, constraints are inequalities or equalities that the variables must satisfy.&lt;SEP&gt;约束条件是指优化问题中限制变量取值的条件，KKT 条件涉及到这类条件的处理。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="目标函数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The objective function is a mathematical function that is to be maximized or minimized in linear programming. It represents the goal of the optimization problem.&lt;SEP&gt;The objective function is the function to be minimized in optimization problems, which includes communication cost in this context.&lt;SEP&gt;目标函数是优化问题中需要极大化或极小化的函数，KKT 条件与目标函数有关。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="顶点解">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A vertex solution is a point that lies on the boundary of the feasible region of a linear programming problem and is a potential solution to the problem. The vertex solutions are the extreme points of the feasible region.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="梯度">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gradient is a vector that points in the direction of the greatest rate of increase of a function, and its magnitude is the rate of increase in that direction.&lt;SEP&gt;The gradient of a function is a vector that points in the direction of the greatest rate of increase of the function. It is the vector of partial derivatives of the function with respect to each of its variables.&lt;SEP&gt;梯度是函数在某一点的切线斜率向量，用于描述函数在该点的局部变化情况。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="线性函数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A linear function is a function whose graph is a straight line. It can be represented by the equation f(x) = mx + b, where m and b are constants. Linear functions are used to model situations where the rate of change is constant.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="无穷小高阶项">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">An infinitesimal high-order term is a term in a mathematical expression that becomes negligible as the variable approaches a certain value. It is often represented by the symbol o(x).</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="几何意义">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The geometric meaning of a concept refers to its interpretation in terms of geometric figures and relationships. It involves visualizing mathematical concepts in terms of shapes, sizes, and positions of geometric objects.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="学习率">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The learning rate is a hyperparameter in gradient descent that determines the step size for each iteration of the algorithm. It controls how much the model parameters are updated in each iteration.&lt;SEP&gt;文中提到的学习率，是梯度下降法中的一个参数。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c5b9cad1a482c29a56b35fc8a645c21c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="参数收敛性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Parameter convergence refers to the behavior of the parameters of a model as the learning process progresses. A model is considered to have converged if its parameters stabilize and no longer change significantly with further iterations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="热传导">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Heat conduction is the transfer of heat through a material due to a temperature difference. It is one of the three primary methods of heat transfer, along with convection and radiation. Heat conduction occurs in solids, liquids, and gases.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="波动方程">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The wave equation is a partial differential equation that describes the propagation of waves. It is used in many areas of physics and engineering to model phenomena such as sound, light, and seismic waves.&lt;SEP&gt;波动方程是描述波动现象的数学方程，常用于物理学和工程学中。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="滤波器设计">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Filter design is the process of creating a filter, which is a device or system that allows certain frequencies to pass through while blocking others. It is used in signal processing to remove unwanted noise from signals.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="频率响应">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Frequency response is the measure of how a system responds to different frequencies of input signals. It is used to analyze and design systems that process signals, such as amplifiers, speakers, and communication systems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="长期平衡分析">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Long-term equilibrium analysis is a method used in economics to study the behavior of economic systems over a long period of time. It involves analyzing the forces that drive the system towards equilibrium and the conditions under which equilibrium is reached.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="单变量序列">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A univariate sequence is a sequence that consists of a single variable. It is a sequence where each term depends only on the index of the term.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="多变量序列">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A multivariate sequence is a sequence that consists of multiple variables. It is a sequence where each term depends on multiple indices or variables.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c24198222afa92c497fa476e00ef81db</data>
</node>
<node id="Loss Function">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Loss Function is a function that measures the difference between the predicted output of the model and the actual output, used to guide the optimization process."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Loss function is a function that measures the difference between the predicted output and the actual output in machine learning.&lt;SEP&gt;The loss function is a critical component in machine learning, specifically in gradient descent methods, which is used for training deep learning models.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a86011fbed05d0890a350d2b791ea51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Deep Learning Model">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Deep learning models are the focus of training in machine learning, where the loss function is minimized to improve the model's performance.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a86011fbed05d0890a350d2b791ea51</data>
</node>
<node id="Gradient Descent Method">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gradient descent is an optimization algorithm used to minimize a function that is critical in the training of deep learning models.</data>
