</node>
<node id="GIS">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">GIS stands for Geographic Information System, which is a system for capturing, storing, analyzing, and managing geospatial data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2204ffef1e97e333dfc5498edbd5ae7b</data>
</node>
<node id="physical simulation">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Physical simulation refers to the use of computer programs to simulate physical phenomena, such as electric fields or gravitational fields.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2204ffef1e97e333dfc5498edbd5ae7b</data>
</node>
<node id="utility function">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Utility function is a concept in economics that represents the satisfaction or benefit a consumer receives from consuming a good or service.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2204ffef1e97e333dfc5498edbd5ae7b</data>
</node>
<node id="production function">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Production function is a concept in economics that shows the relationship between inputs and outputs in the production process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2204ffef1e97e333dfc5498edbd5ae7b</data>
</node>
<node id="edge detection">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Edge detection is a process in image processing that identifies the boundaries of objects in an image.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2204ffef1e97e333dfc5498edbd5ae7b</data>
</node>
<node id="feature extraction">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Feature extraction is the process of selecting the most important features from a set of data to reduce dimensionality and improve the performance of a machine learning model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2204ffef1e97e333dfc5498edbd5ae7b</data>
</node>
<node id="Taylor Series">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">Taylor Series is a mathematical tool for approximating functions using a polynomial expansion, mentioned in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Convergence">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">A property of an optimization algorithm that indicates whether it will eventually find the minimum or maximum of a function.&lt;SEP&gt;Convergence refers to the property of a Taylor series where the remainder term approaches zero, indicating the approximation becomes increasingly accurate.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Maclaurin Series">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">Maclaurin Series is a special case of the Taylor series where the expansion is centered at zero, mentioned in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Derivative">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">Derivative refers to the rate at which one quantity changes with respect to another, mentioned in the context of Taylor series.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Polynomial">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">Polynomial refers to an expression of a finite number of terms, with non-negative integer exponents, mentioned in the context of Taylor series expansion.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Error">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">Error refers to the discrepancy between the actual value of a function and its approximation using a Taylor series, mentioned in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Approximation">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">Approximation refers to the act of estimating or finding a close value to the exact value, mentioned in the context of Taylor series and function approximation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Control Theory">
  <data key="d0">Organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Control Theory is an organization or field of study mentioned in the context of Taylor series applications, possibly related to the design of linear controllers.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Learning">
  <data key="d0">Organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Machine Learning is a field of study that gives computers the ability to learn without being explicitly programmed.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine Learning is an organization or field of study mentioned in the context of Taylor series applications, possibly related to optimization algorithms.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Physics">
  <data key="d0">Organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Physics is an organization or field of study mentioned in the context of Taylor series applications, possibly related to classical mechanics and small angle approximations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Engineering is an organization or field of study mentioned in the context of Taylor series applications, possibly related to numerical analysis and error analysis.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="Numerical Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Numerical Analysis is an organization or field of study mentioned in the context of Taylor series applications, possibly related to numerical integration and differentiation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36fe4da870b3270fb1f58a3814d28304</data>
</node>
<node id="𝜋/6">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">𝜋/6 是 π 的六分之一，是一个常见的角度值，通常表示为 30 度。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="摆动">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">摆动是一种物理现象，通常指物体围绕固定点来回移动。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="函数 𝑓(𝑥) = (𝑎% 𝑥)(𝑏 % 𝑥)">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">函数 𝑓(𝑥) 是一个涉及向量运算的函数，用于表示两个向量的点积。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="Hessian 矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A matrix of second-order partial derivatives of a scalar function, used in second-order optimization methods like Newton's method.&lt;SEP&gt;Hessian matrix is a square matrix of second-order partial derivatives of a scalar-valued function, containing information about the local curvature of the function.&lt;SEP&gt;Hessian 矩阵是二阶偏导数矩阵，用于描述函数的曲率。&lt;SEP&gt;Represents the Hessian matrix of the second derivatives of the loss function, used in Newton's method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-261e2b461646c649ae18e976ba31858f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="目标函数 𝑓(𝑥)">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">目标函数 𝑓(𝑥) 是优化问题中要最小化或最大化的函数。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="约束条件 Ω">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">约束条件 Ω 是优化问题中限制解的条件的集合。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="小角度近似">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">小角度近似是一种数学近似方法，用于在角度较小时简化三角函数的计算。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="sin 𝑥 ≈ 𝑥 − 𝑥^3/3! + 𝑥^5/5! − ...">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">sin 𝑥 的泰勒级数展开式，用于近似计算正弦函数的值。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑥^3/3!">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">𝑥^3/3! 是泰勒级数中的一项，代表正弦函数展开式中的三次项。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑥^5/5!">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">𝑥^5/5! 是泰勒级数中的一项，代表正弦函数展开式中的五次项。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="n-维向量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">n-维向量是一个具有 n 个分量的向量，用于表示空间中的点或方向。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="点积">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">点积是两个向量的乘积，结果是一个标量，表示两个向量的夹角和长度乘积。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="梯度公式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">梯度公式是用于计算函数梯度的数学公式，用于找到函数的局部极值。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="Hessian 矩阵 𝐹(𝑥) = 𝑎𝑏^𝑇 + 𝑏𝑎^𝑇">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Hessian 矩阵 𝐹(𝑥) 是二阶偏导数矩阵，表示函数曲率的矩阵形式。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="常量矩阵">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">常量矩阵是所有元素都是常数的矩阵，其值不随变量变化。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="优化问题的基本形式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">优化问题的基本形式是寻找函数极值的问题，包括最小化和最大化。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="可行域 Ω">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">可行域 Ω 是优化问题中满足约束条件的所有解的集合。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="错误分析">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">错误分析是对错误原因和解决方案的详细研究，用于改进数学推导或计算。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="混淆标量与向量操作">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">混淆标量与向量操作是指错误地将标量运算应用于向量，或反之。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="矩阵与向量乘法结果">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">矩阵与向量乘法结果是指矩阵乘以向量后的结果，通常是一个向量。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4c75943f8ecf574208b9f73f60a1d716</data>
</node>
<node id="f(x)">
  <data key="d0">function</data>
  <data key="d1">f(x) is the objective function of an optimization problem.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="Ω">
  <data key="d0">variable</data>
  <data key="d1">Ω represents the feasible region defined by the constraints of an optimization problem.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="maximization problem">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A maximization problem can be converted into a minimization problem by minimizing the negative of the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="constraint">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Constraints in optimization problems can be classified as having constraints or no constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="convex optimization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Convex optimization refers to optimization problems with convex objective functions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="non-convex optimization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Non-convex optimization refers to optimization problems with non-convex objective functions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="smoothness">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Optimization problems can be smooth or non-smooth based on the smoothness of the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="dimension">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Optimization problems can be one-dimensional (1D) or multidimensional (nD) based on the number of variables.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="relation between gradient and level set">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The tangent vector of the level set is perpendicular to the gradient, and the direction is the fastest path of decrease in the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="second derivative">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Second derivative is used to determine convexity in one dimension: f''(x) &gt; 0 indicates local convexity (local minimum).</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="Hessian matrix">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The Hessian matrix ∇^2f(x) is used to determine convexity in multidimensional problems: a positive definite Hessian matrix indicates local convexity; a negative definite Hessian matrix indicates local concavity.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="machine learning">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Machine learning uses gradient descent and second-order methods as core technologies for training deep learning models.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="engineering design">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Engineering design uses optimization for designing optimal control paths in automation and control.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="economics modeling">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Economics modeling uses optimization to solve optimal consumption or production problems under constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="operations research and data science">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Operations research and data science widely use optimization methods in resource allocation and path planning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="unconstrained optimization problem">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">An unconstrained optimization problem is an optimization problem without constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="one-dimensional function optimization">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">An example of one-dimensional function optimization is finding the minimum value of a function in a given interval.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="Rosenbrock function">
  <data key="d0">function</data>
  <data key="d1">The Rosenbrock function is an example of a non-convex function used in optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="gradient of Rosenbrock function">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The gradient of the Rosenbrock function is a vector that indicates the direction of steepest ascent in the function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="Hessian matrix of Rosenbrock function">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The Hessian matrix of the Rosenbrock function is used to determine the local optima of the function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="local optima of Rosenbrock function">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">The local optima of the Rosenbrock function are points where the gradient is zero and the Hessian matrix is positive definite.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="non-convex optimization problem">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A non-convex optimization problem requires the use of numerical methods to search for global optimal solutions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="constrained optimization problem">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A constrained optimization problem is an optimization problem with constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="analysis of constrained optimization problem">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">The analysis of a constrained optimization problem involves determining whether a critical point is a local minimum, a local maximum, or neither.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="z">
  <data key="d0">variable</data>
  <data key="d1">z is a variable in the optimization function f(x).</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="x1">
  <data key="d0">variable</data>
  <data key="d1">x1 is a variable in the optimization function f(x1, x2).</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="x2">
  <data key="d0">variable</data>
  <data key="d1">x2 is a variable in the optimization function f(x1, x2).</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="c">
  <data key="d0">constant</data>
  <data key="d1">c is a constant in the level set definition S_J = {x | f(x) = c}.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="critical point">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">A critical point is a point where the gradient of the function is zero.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="boundary value">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Boundary value refers to the value of the function at the edges of the feasible region.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="global optimal solution">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">A global optimal solution is the best solution that can be achieved for the optimization problem across the entire feasible region.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="local minimum">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">A local minimum is a point where the function is less than or equal to all nearby points in the feasible region.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="local maximum">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">A local maximum is a point where the function is greater than or equal to all nearby points in the feasible region.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="optimal control path">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Optimal control path is the path that minimizes a cost function in control theory.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="consumption problem">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">A consumption problem is an optimization problem that seeks to maximize utility while satisfying budget constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="production problem">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">A production problem is an optimization problem that seeks to maximize profit while satisfying production constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="resource allocation">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Resource allocation is the process of distributing resources in an optimal way to achieve maximum efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="path planning">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Path planning is the process of finding a path between two points that minimizes a cost function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="numerical methods">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Numerical methods are used to solve optimization problems that cannot be solved analytically.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="Newton's method">
  <data key="d0">method</data>
  <data key="d1">Newton's method is a numerical method for finding the roots of a real-valued function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="quasi-Newton methods">
  <data key="d0">method</data>
  <data key="d1">Quasi-Newton methods are a class of optimization algorithms that approximate the Hessian matrix using limited information.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="interior point">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">An interior point is a point in the feasible region that is not on the boundary.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="boundary point">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">A boundary point is a point on the boundary of the feasible region.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="KKT conditions">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">KKT conditions are a set of necessary conditions for a point to be a local minimum in a constrained optimization problem.&lt;SEP&gt;KKT conditions are optimization conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dc0fbd0f4fadeca6e3a55b410c4f12cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1d8c9e7343cf20cf0c57d99836ff7c</data>
</node>
<node id="约束条件 ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Constraint conditions refer to the conditions that must be met, such as x! ≥ 1 and x# ≥ 2.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="梯度 ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gradient refers to the rate of change of a function and is used to determine the direction of maximum increase or decrease of the function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="目标函数 ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Objective function is the function to be minimized or maximized in an optimization problem.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="局部极小点 ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Local minimum point is a point where the function value is less than or equal to the values at nearby points.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="KKT 条件 ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">KKT conditions are necessary conditions for a local minimum in constrained optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="一阶必要条件 ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">First-order necessary conditions are the conditions that must be satisfied for a point to be a local minimum in an optimization problem.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="二阶必要条件 ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Second-order necessary conditions are the conditions that must be satisfied for a point to be a local minimum in an optimization problem, based on the second derivative of the function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="二阶充分条件 ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Second-order sufficient conditions are the conditions that guarantee a point is a local minimum in an optimization problem, based on the second derivative of the function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="机器学习 ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Machine learning is a field of artificial intelligence that involves the study of algorithms that improve automatically through experience.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="运筹学 ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Operations research is a discipline that deals with the mathematical modeling of complex systems and the analysis of data to determine the best outcome in a given situation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="x!">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">x! is a variable in the constraint condition, referring to the factorial of x.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06057cb16208f863419153b246fa05c5</data>
</node>
<node id="FONC">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">FONC stands for First Order Necessary Conditions, which are necessary but not sufficient conditions for local optimality in optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="SONC">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">SONC stands for Second Order Necessary Conditions, which are also necessary but not sufficient conditions for local optimality in optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="控制工程">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Control engineering is an application field of optimization, used for optimizing control system parameters.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="经济学">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Economics is an application field of optimization, used for solving optimal investment portfolio problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="FONC 和 SONC 易于计算">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The ease of calculating FONC and SONC is a category that includes the fact that they can be computed simply by calculating gradients and Hessian matrices, which is common in convex optimization and linear programming.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="适用于非线性优化问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Applying to nonlinear optimization problems refers to the capability of FONC and SONC to help identify local optimal solutions under unconstrained or constrained conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="理论基础扎实">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The solid theoretical foundation of FONC and SONC refers to their support for many optimization algorithms such as gradient descent and Newton's method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="必要条件非充分">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The necessary but not sufficient nature of the conditions refers to the fact that FONC and SONC are necessary conditions but may not uniquely determine local optimal solutions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="对约束优化问题的局限性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The limitation in constrained optimization problems refers to the need for combining the Lagrange multiplier method when constraints are complex.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="二次函数">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">The example of a simple quadratic function is a specific case of optimization problem discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="非凸目标函数">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">The example of a non-convex objective function is a specific case of optimization problem discussed in the text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="Stationarity">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Stationarity is a part of KKT conditions, referring to the condition that the gradient of the Lagrangian function equals zero.&lt;SEP&gt;Stationarity 是 KKT 条件的一部分，它要求拉格朗日函数的梯度为零，即函数处于平稳状态。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="Primal Feasibility">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A type of feasibility condition that deals with the primal problem's constraints and their satisfaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Primal Feasibility is a part of KKT conditions, referring to the feasibility of the original optimization problem.&lt;SEP&gt;Primal Feasibility 是 KKT 条件的一部分，它要求原始问题中的约束条件得到满足。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Feasibility">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A type of feasibility condition that deals with the dual problem's constraints and their satisfaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual Feasibility is a part of KKT conditions, referring to the feasibility of the dual optimization problem.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual Feasibility 是 KKT 条件的一部分，它要求对偶问题中的约束条件得到满足。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="Complementary Slackness">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A condition in optimization that relates the primal and dual problems, ensuring the feasibility and optimality of the solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Complementary Slackness is a part of KKT conditions, referring to the complementary slackness condition which states that λg(x) = 0 for all i.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="支持向量机（SVM）的优化问题">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">The optimization problem of support vector machines (SVM) is an application of KKT conditions in machine learning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="生产调度、物流优化等含复杂约束的规划问题">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Production scheduling, logistics optimization, and other planning problems with complex constraints are applications of KKT conditions in operations research.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="资源分配、投资组合优化中，KKT 条件可用于建模和求解">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">In resource allocation and portfolio optimization, KKT conditions can be used for modeling and solving problems in economics and financial engineering.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="最优控制问题中，KKT 条件用于处理复杂动态系统的优化">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">In optimal control problems, KKT conditions are used to handle the optimization of complex dynamic systems in control engineering.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="二阶泰勒展开式">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">The second-order Taylor expansion is a mathematical method used to approximate a function by its linear approximation around a given point, involving second derivatives of the function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="损失函数">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">A function that measures the difference between the predicted output and the actual output, used to calculate the gradient during optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Loss function is a function that measures the difference between the predicted output and the actual output in machine learning, used to optimize the model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-261e2b461646c649ae18e976ba31858f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="深度学习模型">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">A class of machine learning models that use neural networks with many layers for feature extraction and transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep learning model is a type of machine learning model that uses a deep neural network with many layers to learn complex patterns in data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-261e2b461646c649ae18e976ba31858f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="路径规划">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Path planning is a process of determining a trajectory for an object to move from one point to another in the most efficient way, often used in robotics and autonomous systems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="资源分配">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Resource allocation is the process of distributing limited resources among competing demands, a common problem in operations research and economics.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="控制系统参数">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Control system parameters are the values that define the behavior of a control system, which can be adjusted to optimize the system's performance.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="最优投资组合问题">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Optimal portfolio problem is a problem in economics that involves selecting an investment portfolio that maximizes expected return for a given level of risk.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="拉格朗日乘子法">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Lagrange multiplier method is a mathematical technique used to find the local maxima and minima of a function subject to equality constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="序列二次规划">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Sequential quadratic programming is an optimization algorithm that solves a series of quadratic programming subproblems to find the optimal solution to a nonlinear programming problem.&lt;SEP&gt;序列二次规划是一种优化算法，它基于 KKT 条件对问题进行求解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="内点法">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Interior-point method is an algorithm for solving convex optimization problems, which iteratively moves a point in the interior of the feasible region towards the optimal solution.&lt;SEP&gt;内点法是一种优化算法，它基于 KKT 条件对问题进行求解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="复杂动态系统">
  <data key="d0">concept</data>
  <data key="d1">Complex dynamic system refers to a system that has a complex behavior that is difficult to predict or analyze, often requiring advanced mathematical tools for optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;复杂动态系统是指具有多个变量和复杂相互作用的系统，KKT 条件用于处理这类系统的优化问题。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476294527e1c59400f3b0cb2686b7ac7</data>
</node>
<node id="KKT 条件">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">KKT 条件是一种用于处理复杂动态系统优化问题的数学方法，能够处理等式和不等式约束问题，适用于大多数非线性规划问题。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="优化算法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Optimization algorithms are discussed in the context of Federated Learning, aiming to solve the distributed optimization problem without centralizing data.&lt;SEP&gt;优化算法是指一系列用于求解优化问题的算法，KKT 条件奠定了对偶理论的基础，在优化算法（如序列二次规划、内点法）中具有重要作用。&lt;SEP&gt;文中提到的优化算法，包括牛顿法和其他可能的优化方法。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5b9cad1a482c29a56b35fc8a645c21c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff7dec96cfa121a0e11b325e13ce1fa</data>
</node>
<node id="局部最优解">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">局部最优解是指优化问题中在某一区域内最优的解，KKT 条件提供了必要条件，有助于判断解的局部最优性。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="全局最优解">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">全局最优解是指优化问题在整个定义域内的最优解，KKT 条件只能提供局部最优解的必要条件，并不能保证全局最优。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="正则性条件">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">正则性条件是应用 KKT 条件时需要满足的条件，如 Slater 条件，以确保 KKT 条件的正确应用。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="Slater 条件">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Slater 条件是 KKT 条件中的一个重要条件，它要求约束条件是严格可行的。&lt;SEP&gt;Slater 条件是应用 KKT 条件时需要满足的正则性条件之一，它要求约束条件是严格可行的。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="等式约束">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">等式约束是指优化问题中需要满足的等式条件，KKT 条件能够处理这类约束问题。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="不等式约束">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">不等式约束是指优化问题中需要满足的不等式条件，KKT 条件能够处理这类约束问题。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="非线性规划问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">非线性规划问题是指目标函数和约束条件至少有一个是非线性的问题，KKT 条件适用于这类问题。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="对偶理论">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">对偶理论是优化理论的一个分支，KKT 条件奠定了这一理论的基础。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="拉格朗日函数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Lagrange function is a function used in optimization to incorporate constraints into the objective function.&lt;SEP&gt;Represents the Lagrange function used to construct the optimization problem with constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;拉格朗日函数是优化理论中的一个工具，用于将约束条件引入目标函数中，KKT 条件与拉格朗日函数有关。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="互补松弛条件">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">互补松弛条件是 KKT 条件的一部分，它描述了约束条件和拉格朗日乘子之间的关系。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="可行性条件">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">可行性条件是优化问题中变量需要满足的条件，KKT 条件包括了对可行性条件的处理。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="对偶可行性条件">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">对偶可行性条件是 KKT 条件的一部分，它描述了对偶问题中的可行性条件。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="严格可行性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">严格可行性是指约束条件在某个区域内严格满足，Slater 条件是这种可行性的一个例子。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="变量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">变量是优化问题中需要确定其值的参数，KKT 条件涉及到变量的处理。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="拉格朗日乘子">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">拉格朗日乘子是 KKT 条件中用于处理约束条件的参数，它反映了约束条件对目标函数的影响。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="非平凡解">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">非平凡解是指优化问题中目标函数不为零的解，KKT 条件与非平凡解有关。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="平凡解">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">平凡解是指优化问题中目标函数为零的解，KKT 条件与平凡解有关。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="多变量优化问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">多变量优化问题是指有多个变量的优化问题，KKT 条件适用于这类问题。&lt;SEP&gt;多变量优化问题是指有多个变量的优化问题，KKT 条�件适用于这类问题。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="单变量优化问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">单变量优化问题是指只有一个变量的优化问题，KKT 条件可以应用于这类问题的求解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="最小化问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">最小化问题是指寻找目标函数最小值的优化问题，KKT 条件可以应用于这类问题的求解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="最大化问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">最大化问题是指寻找目标函数最大值的优化问题，KKT 条件可以应用于这类问题的求解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="线性规划问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">线性规划问题是指目标函数和约束条件都是线性的优化问题，KKT 条件可以应用于这类问题的求解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="非线性优化问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">非线性优化问题是指目标函数和约束条件至少有一个是非线性的优化问题，KKT 条件可以应用于这类问题的求解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="连续优化问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">连续优化问题是指目标函数和约束条件都是连续的优化问题，KKT 条件可以应用于这类问题的求解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="离散优化问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">离散优化问题是指目标函数和约束条件至少有一个是离散的优化问题，KKT 条件可以应用于这类问题的求解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="非凸优化问题">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">非凸优化问题是指目标函数和约束条件至少有一个是非凸的优化问题，KKT 条件可以应用于这类问题的求解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73d671cafe9b6639b0941c92099c62cd</data>
</node>
<node id="Feasibility Condition">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">A specific category of conditions in optimization problems, concerning the constraints and their satisfaction.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="Steady State Equation">
  <data key="d0">Event</data>
  <data key="d1">An equation derived from the steady state conditions of an optimization problem, which is used to find the solution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="Optimization Problem">
  <data key="d0">Event</data>
  <data key="d1">An optimization problem is a mathematical problem defined by an objective function and constraints, where the objective is to find the values of the variables that minimize or maximize the objective function.&lt;SEP&gt;The problem being solved in the text, which involves finding the optimal solution under certain constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="KKT Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Feasibility Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">A set of necessary conditions for a local optimum in a constrained optimization problem, named after Kuhn and Tucker.&lt;SEP&gt;KKT Conditions are used to analyze the balance between personalized models and the global model in constrained optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="Optimal Solution">
  <data key="d0">Event</data>
  <data key="d1">The solution to the optimization problem that satisfies all constraints and optimizes the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="Directional Derivative">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">A derivative of a function in the direction of a given vector, used to describe the rate of change of the function in that direction.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="Gradient Descent Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Event</data>
  <data key="d1">An optimization algorithm that uses the negative gradient of the loss function to find the minimum of a function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="Step Size">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">A parameter in optimization algorithms that determines the size of the steps taken in the direction of steepest descent or ascent.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="Convexity">
  <data key="d0">Category</data>
  <data key="d1">A property of a function that is curved outward in both directions from any point on the graph, indicating that the function has a single minimum or maximum.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3099892f0fe8160f517d357acb20d6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="长选择">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The concept of long selection involves careful consideration of step size to avoid slow convergence or divergence.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="收敛">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Convergence refers to the process of the algorithm approaching a minimum or optimal solution in optimization problems.&lt;SEP&gt;文中提到的收敛，是牛顿法求解优化问题的目标，即找到最优解。</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c5b9cad1a482c29a56b35fc8a645c21c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="发散">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Divergence in optimization indicates that the algorithm is moving away from a minimum or optimal solution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="线搜索方法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Line search methods include golden section search, Newton's method, and bisection method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="收敛性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Convergence property of gradient descent is that it converges to the global minimum under smooth and convex objective functions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="效率">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Efficiency of gradient descent is that it is simple to implement but may have slow convergence in ill-conditioned problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="机器学习与深度学习">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Machine learning and deep learning are fields where gradient descent is used for training neural networks.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="经济学与金融建模">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Economics and financial modeling use gradient descent for optimal portfolio selection and risk management.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="工程与运筹学">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Engineering and operations research apply gradient descent in path planning and system optimization.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="算法简单">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The simplicity of the gradient descent algorithm is that it only requires the computation of the gradient of the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="通用性强">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The strong generality of gradient descent is that it is widely applicable to unconstrained optimization problems, especially convex optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="扩展性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The extensibility of gradient descent allows combining different step size strategies and optimization methods to improve performance.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="对初值敏感">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gradient descent is sensitive to the initial value, and an inappropriate choice may lead to convergence to a local minimum.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="步长选择难">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Choosing an appropriate step size is difficult in gradient descent, as an inappropriate step size may lead to divergence or slow convergence.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="条件数影响">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The condition number affects the convergence speed of gradient descent, as a larger condition number can significantly slow down convergence.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="目标函数 𝒇(𝒙, 𝒚) = 𝒙𝟐 + 𝒚𝟐">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">The example of the objective function f(x, y) = x^2 + y^2 demonstrates the gradient descent process with a specific initial point and step size.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="目标函数 𝒇(𝒙) = 𝒙𝟒 − 𝟑𝒙𝟑 + 𝟐">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">The example of the objective function f(x) = x^4 - 3x^3 + 2 illustrates the gradient descent process with a specific initial point and step size.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="梯度下降法的特点">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The characteristics of gradient descent include moving along the normal direction of the contour lines and inefficient paths that do not directly approach the global optimal point.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="收敛慢">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The slow convergence of gradient descent is due to the zigzag path, especially when the contour lines are elliptical, leading to alternating iterations along the main axis.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="对步长敏感">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gradient descent is sensitive to the step size, and an inappropriate choice can significantly affect convergence speed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="局部特性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gradient descent only uses first-order information of the objective function (gradient) and cannot fully utilize the curvature information (Hessian) of the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="黄金分割法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Golden section search is a line search method used to find the minimum of a unimodal function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="二分法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Bisection method is a root-finding method that repeatedly bisects an interval and then selects a subinterval in which a root exists.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="目标函数 𝒇(𝒙, 𝒚) = 𝒙𝟐 + 𝒚𝟐 的梯度计算">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The gradient calculation of the objective function f(x, y) = x^2 + y^2 involves finding the partial derivatives with respect to x and y.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="更新公式">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The update formula for gradient descent involves subtracting a fraction of the gradient from the current point to move towards the minimum.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="收敛过程">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The convergence process of gradient descent shows how the algorithm approaches the minimum over a series of iterations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="目标函数 𝒇(𝒙) = 𝒙𝟒 − 𝟑𝒙𝟑 + 𝟐 的梯度计算">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The gradient calculation of the objective function f(x) = x^4 - 3x^3 + 2 involves finding the derivative with respect to x.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="更新公式：𝑥&amp;+! = 𝑥&amp; − 𝛼𝑓 , (𝑥&amp; )">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The update formula for gradient descent in the example with f(x) = x^4 - 3x^3 + 2 shows how the algorithm updates the x-coordinate based on the derivative and step size.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="收敛过程：取初始点 𝑥: = 1.5，步长 𝛼 = 0.01">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The convergence process example with f(x) = x^4 - 3x^3 + 2 takes an initial point x0 = 1.5 and a step size α = 0.01 to illustrate the gradient descent iterations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="图 6.1 梯度下降法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Figure 6.1 illustrates the gradient descent method showing the path of iteration along the normal direction of the contour lines.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="路径不高效">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The inefficient path of gradient descent is characterized by frequent changes in direction, not directly approaching the global optimal point.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="局部特性：梯度下降法只利用目标函数的一阶信息（梯度），无法充分利用目标函数的曲率信息（Hessian）">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The local property of gradient descent is that it only uses first-order information of the objective function (gradient) and cannot fully utilize the curvature information (Hessian) of the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="条件数 𝜅（Hessian 矩阵特征值最大值与最小值的比值）">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The condition number κ (the ratio of the largest to the smallest eigenvalue of the Hessian matrix) is a measure of the ill-conditioning of a matrix.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1daed866d8750642dcecc03dc8933344</data>
</node>
<node id="Step Length α">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Step Length α is a variable that significantly affects convergence speed in optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Convergence Speed">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Convergence Speed refers to how quickly an optimization problem approaches a solution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Gradient Descent">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gradient Descent is an optimization algorithm that uses first-order information (gradient) of the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Hessian">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Hessian is a matrix of second-order partial derivatives of a scalar-valued function, defining the local curvature of the function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Local Optimum">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Local Optimum is a point in multidimensional space that is a local extremum of a given function, and is a solution of a system of equations, or a point at which the function's value is neither a local maximum nor a local minimum.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Newton's Method">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Newton's Method is an optimization algorithm that uses second-order derivatives to find the minimum or maximum of a function, and is applied in the distributed Newton method for federated learning.&lt;SEP&gt;Newton's Method is an optimization method that uses second-order information (Hessian) of the objective function to accelerate convergence.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Preconditioning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Preconditioning is a process that improves the convergence rate of an algorithm by transforming a matrix into a more favorable form.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Momentum Method">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Momentum Method is an optimization technique that introduces a momentum term to make the iteration points move more smoothly towards the optimal solution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptive Step Size Method">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Adaptive Step Size Method is a technique that uses line search technology or optimization algorithms like Adam to automatically adjust the step size.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Deep Learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Deep Learning is a subset of machine learning that structures algorithms in layers to create an "artificial neural network" that can learn from large amounts of data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="L-BFGS Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">L-BFGS Algorithm is a limited-memory Quasi-Newton method for large-scale optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Design">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Structural Design is the process of planning and designing a structure or object, ensuring safety, serviceability, and aesthetics.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Control">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Automatic Control is the application of control theory and engineering to the design, construction, and analysis of systems that operate automatically.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Economics and Finance">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Economics and Finance is the study of how individuals, businesses, and governments make decisions on allocating resources to achieve desired ends.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Physics and Chemistry">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Physics and Chemistry are scientific disciplines that study the behavior of matter and energy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Objective Function">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Objective function is the function to be minimized or maximized in an optimization problem.&lt;SEP&gt;The objective function is a function to be minimized or maximized in an optimization problem.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Saddle Point">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A saddle point is a point on the surface of a function where the function has a local minimum in one direction and a local maximum in another direction.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Global Optimum">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The global optimum is the best possible solution to an optimization problem, where the objective function is minimized or maximized over the entire problem domain.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Line Search Technology">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Line search technology is a method used to find the optimal step size in optimization algorithms by searching along a line in the direction of the gradient or descent direction.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Adam Optimization Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Adam is an optimization algorithm that combines the best properties of the AdaGrad and RMSProp algorithms, which are adaptive learning rate methods for stochastic optimization.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Condition Number">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The condition number of a matrix is a measure of how sensitive the solution of a system of linear equations is to changes in the coefficients of the system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Second-Order Optimization Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A second-order optimization algorithm is an optimization algorithm that uses second-order information (second derivatives) of the objective function to improve the convergence rate and accuracy of the optimization process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Quasi-Newton Method">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A Quasi-Newton method is an optimization algorithm that approximates the second derivative of the objective function using limited information, allowing it to be applied to problems where the Hessian matrix is expensive to compute or not available.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Limited-Memory Quasi-Newton Method">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A limited-memory Quasi-Newton method is a variant of the Quasi-Newton method that uses a limited amount of memory to store the second derivatives, making it suitable for large-scale optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Stochastic Optimization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Stochastic optimization is a class of optimization algorithms that use random search techniques to find the optimal solution to a problem, rather than relying on gradient information.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptive Learning Rate Methods">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Adaptive learning rate methods are optimization algorithms that adjust the learning rate during the optimization process to improve convergence and accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</node>
