</node>
<node id="Proximal Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">technology</data>
  <data key="d1">Proximal Algorithm is a method for solving optimization problems with regularization terms, often used in convex optimization problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Proximal Algorithm is a method used to solve optimization problems with constraints, which is applied in the optimization of federated learning with L1 regularization.&lt;SEP&gt;Proximal Algorithm is an algorithm used in FedProx.&lt;SEP&gt;This is an algorithm that reduces communication frequency by performing local Proximal updates.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53e7e73846d2eaaea200c6f3139c38fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fbd0f4fadeca6e3a55b410c4f12cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
