  <data key="d2">chunk-261e2b461646c649ae18e976ba31858f</data>
</node>
<node id="异步更新">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">An update mechanism in federated learning where clients can update their models independently of each other.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-261e2b461646c649ae18e976ba31858f</data>
</node>
<node id="分布式计算">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">A computing paradigm that involves performing a task across multiple computing resources in a distributed manner.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-261e2b461646c649ae18e976ba31858f</data>
</node>
<node id="模型收敛">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The process by which a model's performance improves over time as it learns from the training data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-261e2b461646c649ae18e976ba31858f</data>
</node>
<node id="Hessian Matrix">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">The Hessian Matrix is a mathematical tool used in optimization, specifically in the context of the Hessian-based optimization methods for federated learning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Distributed Newton Method">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Distributed Newton Method is an optimization technique used in federated learning to aggregate gradients and Hessian matrices from multiple clients to perform Newton updates, which is suitable for data distributed over a wide area.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Regularization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Regularization is a technique used in machine learning to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty to the loss function, which is applied in the distributed regularization optimization in federated learning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="L1 Regularization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">L1 Regularization, also known as Lasso, is a form of regularization that encourages sparsity in the coefficients of a model, which is used in the proximal algorithm with L1 regularization in federated learning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Client">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Client refers to the individual or entity that participates in the federated learning process, contributing data and computations."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Server">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Server in the context of federated learning is the central entity that coordinates the training process and aggregates the updates from clients."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Data">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Data is the raw information that clients provide for training the model in federated learning."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Model">
  <data key="d0">organization</data>
  <data key="d1">Model is the machine learning model that is being trained across multiple clients in the federated learning process."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Local Loss Function">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Local Loss Function is the loss function used by each client to measure the performance of its local model."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Global Loss Function">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Global Loss Function is the loss function that is optimized across all clients in the federated learning process."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Communication">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Communication refers to the process of exchanging information between the server and clients in federated learning."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Privacy">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Privacy is a key concern in federated learning, as it involves training a model using data from multiple clients without sharing the raw data."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Security">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Security is a concern in federated learning, as the communication between clients and the server must be secure to protect the data and the model."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Scalability">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Scalability refers to the ability of the federated learning system to handle an increasing number of clients and data points."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Efficiency is a measure of how well the federated learning system performs in terms of computation and communication."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Model Aggregation">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Model Aggregation is the process of combining the local models from all clients into a single global model in federated learning."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="Client Update">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">Client Update is the process by which each client receives the global model and updates its local model based on the new global model."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c5c912f6b46d4dd53664780b33bb589</data>
</node>
<node id="ℓ1 regularization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">ℓ1 regularization is a form of regularization used in optimization to control the size of the coefficients in a model, particularly useful in high-dimensional data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="proximal operator">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Proximal operator is used in optimization to solve problems with constraints, often in combination with gradient descent.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="federated learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Federated learning is a machine learning framework where the training of a shared model is distributed across multiple clients, each holding a portion of the data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="ℓ1">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">ℓ1 refers to the absolute value of the magnitude of the coefficients in a linear model, which is the measure used in ℓ1 regularization.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="gradient descent">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gradient descent is an optimization algorithm that finds the minimum of a function by iteratively moving in the direction of the negative gradient of the function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="proximal gradient descent">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Proximal gradient descent is a variant of gradient descent that incorporates a proximal operator to enforce constraints, such as those imposed by regularization.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="microscopic communication efficiency optimization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Microscopic communication efficiency optimization refers to the optimization of communication within the context of distributed learning algorithms.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="macroscopic communication cost optimization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Macroscopic communication cost optimization refers to the optimization of overall communication cost in distributed learning, considering the sum of communication costs across all clients.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="Top-k gradient selection">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Top-k gradient selection is a technique to reduce communication cost by sending only the top-k gradients in magnitude, where k is a predefined parameter.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="quantization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Quantization is a process of reducing the precision of data to a lower level, which can be used to compress gradients and reduce communication cost.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="sparse vector">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Sparse vector is a vector with a large number of zeros, which is common in high-dimensional data and can be used to represent sparse features.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="communication cost constraint">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Communication cost constraint is a constraint imposed on the communication cost in distributed learning, ensuring that the total communication does not exceed a certain limit.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f00f00a3a5eeee63105409d939e3f519</data>
</node>
<node id="分布式优化方法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">This refers to a method that includes communication cost in the objective function, aiming to optimize for communication efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="梯度压缩">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gradient compression is a method where only part of the gradient update is transmitted, and gradients are quantized to a lower precision.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="局部训练多轮">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">This technique involves multiple rounds of local gradient descent before each communication to reduce the frequency of communication.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="差分更新">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">This method transmits only the difference in model updates to reduce communication.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="KKT 条件的通信约束">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">This refers to incorporating communication constraints into the optimization problem using KKT conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="差分隐私">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">This is a privacy mechanism used in federated learning to protect user data by adding noise to the global model update.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="有约束优化的差分隐私">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">This method adds privacy constraints to the optimization target to protect user data and maintain optimization precision.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="拉格朗日松弛法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Lagrange relaxation is a method used to relax constraints in optimization problems, often used in conjunction with KKT conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Lagrange relaxation is a technique used in optimization to relax constraints by introducing additional variables.&lt;SEP&gt;This is a method used to construct a Lagrange function for constrained optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="投影法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Projection method is used to enforce constraints by projecting variables onto a constraint set.&lt;SEP&gt;This method projects the parameters back into the constrained set after each model update.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="通信代价">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Communication cost refers to the expense associated with data transmission in distributed optimization methods.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="权重">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The weight 𝛾 is a parameter that determines the importance of communication cost in the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="模型参数">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Model parameters are the variables that define the model's structure and are updated during optimization processes.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="更新">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Update refers to the process of adjusting model parameters based on the optimization algorithm.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="局部梯度下降">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Local gradient descent is a method used by clients to optimize their local models before communication.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="全局同步">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Global synchronization is the process of updating the global model with the aggregated updates from all clients.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="拉普拉斯噪声">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Laplace noise is a type of noise added to the global model update to ensure differential privacy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="高斯噪声">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gaussian noise is a type of noise added to the global model update to ensure differential privacy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="隐私预算">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Privacy budget is a measure of the amount of noise that can be added to the model update before privacy is compromised.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="模型性能">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Model performance refers to the effectiveness of the model in making accurate predictions or decisions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="优化精度">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Optimization precision refers to the level of accuracy in the optimization process, which can be affected by noise added for privacy protection.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="对偶乘子">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Dual variable is a variable used in optimization to handle constraints, often in the context of KKT conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="模型参数空间">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Model parameter space is the set of all possible values that model parameters can take.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="约束">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Constraints are conditions that must be satisfied during the optimization process, such as privacy constraints in differential privacy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="参数更新范围">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Parameter update range refers to the allowable changes in model parameters during the optimization process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="对偶法">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The dual method is an optimization technique that involves transforming a primal optimization problem into a dual problem.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="参数投影">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Parameter projection is the process of projecting model parameters back into a feasible region after each update.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="差分隐私度量">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Differential privacy measure is a way to quantify the level of privacy protection provided by differential privacy techniques.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="隐私保护强度">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Privacy protection strength refers to the degree to which user data is protected from unauthorized access or analysis.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="有约束优化的个性化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">This is a method of personalizing models while still adhering to constraints, such as privacy constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81cb9bc58fbb6b43753e03e568548331</data>
</node>
<node id="𝜆">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">𝜆 is a parameter representing the constraint on the dual multiplier in optimization problems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Projection Method">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Projection Method is a technique to project parameters back into a constrained set after each model update.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Constrained Optimization for Personalized Federated Learning">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">In personalized federated learning, each client may need a personalized model 𝑤&amp; rather than a shared global model, with optimization objectives involving constraints on the personalized model's deviation from the global model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Alternating Optimization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Alternating Optimization is an optimization method where the global model and each client's personalized model are optimized alternately.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Regularization Method">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Regularization Method transforms constraints into regularization terms to redefine the objective function for personalized optimization.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Newton's Method for Personalized Federated Learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Newton's Method can accelerate local model optimization and is effective for optimizing personalized objective functions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Subgradient Method for Client Updates">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Subgradient Method is used to update the client models in a regularized optimization problem, encouraging sparse updates to the personalized model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Shrinkage Operator for Personalized Model Optimization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Shrinkage Operator is used to optimize personalized models by promoting sparsity and balancing consistency with the global model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Proximal Algorithm for Model Personalization (Per-FedAvg)">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Proximal Algorithm is used to personalize models in federated learning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Multiplier">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">The dual multiplier is a concept in optimization used to transform a primal problem into a dual problem.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Gradient Update">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Gradient update is a method to update model parameters based on the gradient of the loss function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Constrained Set">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Constrained set is the set of values that a parameter must belong to, as defined by the constraints of the optimization problem.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Global Model">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Global model is the shared model in federated learning that all clients aim to optimize while preserving privacy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Client Model">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Client model is the personalized model specific to each client in federated learning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Deviation Constraint">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Deviation constraint is a constraint that limits how much a personalized model can deviate from the global model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Constraint Term">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Constraint term is a term in the objective function that represents the penalty for violating a constraint.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Regularization Term">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Regularization term is a term added to the objective function to prevent overfitting and encourage generalization.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Local Loss">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Local loss is the loss computed on the client's local dataset during federated learning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Global Loss">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Global loss is the aggregated loss across all clients in federated learning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Regularization Parameter">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Regularization parameter is a hyperparameter that controls the strength of the regularization term in the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Sparse Regularization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Sparse regularization is a type of regularization that encourages the model parameters to be sparse, meaning many of them are zero.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="Proximal Point Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Proximal Point Algorithm is a method for solving optimization problems by minimizing the sum of a smooth function and a non-smooth regularization term.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bff4b6b0014283ad3c5e684ce7a25986</data>
</node>
<node id="稀疏化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Refers to the process of reducing the dimensionality of a data set by eliminating redundant or irrelevant features.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="个性化与全局模型的一致性">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Addresses the balance between personalization and consistency across a global model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑤&amp;">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Symbolizes a variable or parameter in a mathematical model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑆j">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents a specific component or element in the model, possibly a feature or data point.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="𝜂">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents the learning rate in the context of the provided text.&lt;SEP&gt;Symbolizes the learning rate in an optimization algorithm, determining the step size of parameter updates.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b70a45587e0757d21f98b0f35e3f0ad3</data>
</node>
<node id="∇𝐹&amp; (𝑤&amp; )">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Denotes the gradient of the loss function with respect to the parameter 𝑤&amp;.&lt;SEP&gt;∇𝐹&amp; (𝑤&amp; ) is the gradient of the local loss function with respect to the model parameters.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fbd0f4fadeca6e3a55b410c4f12cf</data>
</node>
<node id="𝜆𝑤global ">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents a regularization term that promotes consistency with the global model 𝑤global.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="Proximal Algorithm 模型个性化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Describes a technique for personalizing a model while maintaining consistency with a global model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="局部优化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Involves updating the personalized model on each client using the Proximal Gradient method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="全局聚合">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Involves updating the global model on the server side using aggregated updates from all clients.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="有约束优化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Involves optimizing the global model with constraints on the clients' computational or communication resources.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="KKT 条件优化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Involves incorporating KKT conditions to optimize the global model while respecting client resource constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="Shrinkage Operato 的异构设备资源约束优化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Involves using a Shrinkage Operator to optimize the model for devices with varying computational and storage resources.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="KKT 条件优化 Non-IID 数据">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Describes a method to optimize for Non-IID data by incorporating KKT conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="牛顿法的正则化优化">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Involves regularizing the objective function and using Newton's method to optimize for Non-IID data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="ℓ&amp; (𝑤)">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents the local loss function for client 𝑘.&lt;SEP&gt;ℓ&amp; (𝑤) is the local loss function for client 𝑘.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fbd0f4fadeca6e3a55b410c4f12cf</data>
</node>
<node id="‖𝑤 − 𝑤global ‖#">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents a regularization term that encourages the local model to be close to the global model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="g+!">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents an iteration step in the optimization process.&lt;SEP&gt;g+! represents the (g+1)th iteration.&lt;SEP&gt;g+! represents the next iteration in the optimization process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fbd0f4fadeca6e3a55b410c4f12cf</data>
</node>
<node id="g">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents the current iteration step in the optimization process.&lt;SEP&gt;g is an iteration variable in the optimization process.&lt;SEP&gt;g represents the gth iteration.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fbd0f4fadeca6e3a55b410c4f12cf</data>
</node>
<node id="e">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents the iteration number in the context of the provided text.&lt;SEP&gt;Represents the total number of clients participating in the federated learning process.&lt;SEP&gt;e is a regularization term in the objective function.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b70a45587e0757d21f98b0f35e3f0ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fbd0f4fadeca6e3a55b410c4f12cf</data>
</node>
<node id="p&amp;">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents the proportion of the data or samples contributed by client 𝑘.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑅&amp;">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents the resource limit of client 𝑘, which could be computational or communication resources.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ead56231c879e9b3817d4e56ec1f8515</data>
</node>
<node id="𝑅max,&amp;">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Represents the maximum resource limit among all clients.</data>
