<edge source="DeMorgan's Law" target="A and B">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">De Morgan's Law establishes that the negation of a conjunction (A and B) is equivalent to the disjunction of the negations (not A or not B).</data>
  <data key="d5">logical equivalence, DeMorgan's Law</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</edge>
<edge source="DeMorgan's Law" target="not (A or B)">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">De Morgan's Law indicates that the negation of a disjunction (A or B) is equivalent to the conjunction of the negations (not A and not B).</data>
  <data key="d5">logical equivalence, DeMorgan's Law</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</edge>
<edge source="A ⟹ B" target="not A or B">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">The conditional statement A implies B is logically equivalent to not A or B, according to De Morgan's Law.</data>
  <data key="d5">logical equivalence, DeMorgan's Law</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</edge>
<edge source="A" target="B">
  <data key="d3">16.0</data>
  <data key="d4">In logical operations, A and B are often used as placeholders for propositions or conditions that can be combined or compared.&lt;SEP&gt;原命题表明如果A成立，则B也成立，这是逻辑推理的基础。</data>
  <data key="d5">logical operation, placeholder&lt;SEP&gt;条件推理</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</edge>
<edge source="A" target="Category">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">The variable 'A' is related to the 'Category' of mathematics as it represents a matrix."|&gt;"matrix representation</data>
  <data key="d5">7</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c70a5219fa0a439a10ed3024ed1964a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="A" target="Ax=b">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">Matrix A, which includes vectors a! and a', forms the basis for the linear equation system Ax=b, where x' is the solution vector.</data>
  <data key="d5">equation system, matrix basis</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="B" target="Ax=b">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">Matrix B is used in the linear equation system Ax=b, where it is invertible to find the solution vector x'.</data>
  <data key="d5">equation system, matrix inversion</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2059dcc632561ac949238a8ff6034bc6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="conjunction" target="disjunction">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">Conjunction and disjunction are two different logical operations that can be used to combine propositions.</data>
  <data key="d5">logical operation, combination</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</edge>
<edge source="implication" target="equivalence">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">Implication and equivalence are two different logical relationships that can be used to describe the relationship between propositions.</data>
  <data key="d5">logical relationship, description</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</edge>
<edge source="inference" target="conclusion">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">A conclusion is the result of inference, derived from premises or evidence.</data>
  <data key="d5">inference, result</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</edge>
<edge source="deduction" target="induction">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">Deduction and induction are two different forms of inference that can be used to derive conclusions from premises.</data>
  <data key="d5">inference, form</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</edge>
<edge source="axiom" target="postulate">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">An axiom and a postulate are both fundamental assumptions or propositions that serve as the basis for logical reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d5">logical reasoning, foundation</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</edge>
<edge source="rule" target="premise">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">A rule is a principle that governs behavior or action, and a premise is a statement that is assumed to be true and serves as a basis for an argument or conclusion.</data>
  <data key="d5">logical reasoning, basis</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fafdfdb136157285f7a8d276a2b14346</data>
</edge>
<edge source="成立" target="不成立">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">原命题和逆否命题在逻辑上是等价的，即如果原命题成立，则逆否命题也成立。</data>
  <data key="d5">逻辑等价</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="不成立" target="不成立">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">逆否命题表明如果B不成立，则A也不成立，这是逻辑推理的逆否形式。</data>
  <data key="d5">逆否推理</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="逆否命题" target="逆否命题法">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">逆否命题法通过证明逆否命题来证明原命题。</data>
  <data key="d5">逆否推理</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d94af26a5f821b0759f8bb162bc7c5e6</data>
</edge>
