</edge>
<edge source="Gradient Descent" target="Hessian">
  <data key="d3">6.0</data>
  <data key="d4">Gradient Descent only utilizes the first-order information (gradient) of the objective function, and cannot fully utilize the curvature information (Hessian) of the function, which may lead to poor performance in complex optimization problems (such as near saddle points).</data>
  <data key="d5">optimization, information utilization</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50f15e4e7e2e5d4a402eea2e94ad742c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gradient Descent" target="Local Optimum">
  <data key="d3">5.0</data>
