</edge>
<edge source="‖x − b‖ " target="x^* ">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">The norm of the difference between x and b is a component of the objective function that is minimized to find the optimal solution x^*."|&gt;"objective function, minimization</data>
  <data key="d5">8</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47d799488921d39a7d144085504292d8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="‖x‖ " target="x^* ">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">The norm of x is part of the objective function in optimization, and the optimal solution x^* will minimize this norm."|&gt;"objective function, minimization</data>
  <data key="d5">8</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47d799488921d39a7d144085504292d8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2λ " target="x^* ">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
