  <data key="d5">7</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47d799488921d39a7d144085504292d8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sgn(b) " target="max{">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">The sign function sgn(b) is used in the proximity operator formula, which involves the max function to ensure the non-negativity of the optimal solution x^*."|&gt;"proximity operator, non-negativity</data>
  <data key="d5">7</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47d799488921d39a7d144085504292d8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="max{" target="|b| ">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">The absolute value of b is used in the proximity operator formula, which is part of the max function to calculate the optimal solution x^*."|&gt;"proximity operator, optimization</data>
  <data key="d5">7</data>
